{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game","id":1212634,"title":"The Conan books read like an Exalted game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-28T06:44:09-07:00","id":1212634,"title":"The Conan books read like an Exalted game","content":"I know, this isn't news. It's not like the Conan books haven't been referenced throughout the history of the line. Most relevantly there was the third edition statement that the sorcery rewrite was heavily influenced by them. \u200bBut I'd never exposed myself to Conan aside from the movies (when they came out, I'm not as young as all that). I recently found a complete e-book collection for $0.99, and I've read the first few novellas. I was shocked at how well everything, yes everything, in the books fit within scope and tone of Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T06:47:57-07:00","id":1212637,"title":"","content":"There needs to be an initiation in which the user is the brother in spirit of a potent demon, with a weakness in which the destruction of one kills the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:03:40-07:00","id":1212736,"title":"","content":"I agree that 3e and sword &amp; sorcery novels share some common elements. One among many - their independence from Tolkien's opus.<br /> <br /> I think it's also worth mentioning, if probably old news, that many of those novels were racist, sexist, homophobic... in general, some of their main aspects were almost the opposite of Exalted.<br /> <br /> It seems to me Exalted took some interesting elements from sword &amp; sorcery and then turned them on their head... while leaving others quite similar.<br /> <br /> The result is that Exalted is definitely a product of our times, and more often than not plays to our sensibilities... while s&amp;s usually does the opposite.<br /> <br /> It can still be interesting to contrast and compare the two, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T13:19:26-07:00","id":1212773,"title":"","content":"Robert E. Howard's work and race are an interesting and nuanced topic, as he is a good example of someone who meant well, but was also irreparably a product of his time (in contrast with his friend H.P. Lovecraft, who was ideologically a passionate racist by the standards of his own contemporaries).<br /> <br /> (And yes, I recognize that someone &quot;meaning well&quot; while still being friends and supporting the work of a passionate ideological racist is white privilege in action, as it represents the ability to treat racial politics as an abstract topic of debate rather than an imminent reality that destroys lives)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-28-2018, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T15:26:16-07:00","id":1212815,"title":"","content":"Just because an author was racist, or sexist, or homophobic or whatever, doesn't meant that you aren't allowed to enjoy their work. There are lots of authors (and movie directors and actors, etc) who are complete scum but have produced wonderful works nevertheless, and it's always important to remember that just because someone reads and enjoys aspects of such a scummy person's work doesn't mean that they agree with or like any of the more personal aspects of the creators actions or beliefs.*<br /> <br /> Anyway I think Apromor is correct in that virtually any situation that occurs in Conan could almost play out in an identical fashion in Exalted, which is pretty cool. Conan has always been a huge inspiration for the Exalted setting.<br /> <br /> *This isn't really directed at anyone in specific, but I've seen lots of situations online where someone says, &quot;I really enjoyed X!&quot; and then people say, &quot;Yeah but the guy who made it is a scumbag,&quot; and the original poster ends up feeling like he's being attacked for supporting the actions of the creator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T15:31:41-07:00","id":1212818,"title":"","content":"Oh of course, but it does impact that work and is thus relevant to discussion of said work. Lovecraft\u2019s virulent racism, and Howard\u2019s limited lens of his time are in the texts not separate personal notes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T16:52:38-07:00","id":1212839,"title":"","content":"Honestly, IMO, Conan is kind of weird racially in ways that are pretty specific to it, waaay beyond what early Sword and Sorcery is generally. Like, the whole history in &quot;The Hyborian Age&quot; is pretty much a history of racial conflicts between peoples, racial degeneration / decline. No exaggeration, you can read it here - <a href=\"http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks06/0603571.txt\" target=\"_blank\">http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks06/0603571.txt</a>. (The history also doesn't really make any economic, technological or social sense whatsoever.) Characterization in stories is really oriented towards whatever fantasy human race each character is. You don't really get that in Clark Ashton Smith or Fritz Leiber or other such early people at all. As adventure stories, of course they're influential for... reasons, but while I'm far from at the higher level of concern about these sorts of issues in daily life (or probably even at the middle, in truth), I still found most of them borderline unreadable (in the sense of &quot;What the hell is all this rambling nonsense? Why am I reading this?&quot;.).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T16:55:21-07:00","id":1212840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1212773#post1212773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robert E. Howard's work and race are an interesting and nuanced topic, as he is a good example of someone who meant well, but was also irreparably a product of his time (in contrast with his friend H.P. Lovecraft, who was ideologically a passionate racist by the standards of his own contemporaries).<br /> <br /> (And yes, I recognize that someone &quot;meaning well&quot; while still being friends and supporting the work of a passionate ideological racist, is white privilege in action, as it represents the ability to treat racial politics as an abstract topic of debate rather than a an imminent reality that destroys lives)</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't understand how Lovecraft married a Jew while staying so bigoted against them without getting divorced. Was his wife a masochist or something?<br /> <br /> Edit: I have discovered that they did in fact get divorced, never mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:36:25-07:00","id":1213039,"title":"","content":"I'd like to specify I'm not in fact telling anyone what to read or not to read, nor am I accusing anyone who enjoys the works of notoriously racist, or misogyinist, or whatever, authors, that they automatically partake of those authors' views and are horrible people and it's badwrong fun.<br /> <br /> I like Game of Thrones. It's sexist, racist, rather homophobic and that's probably not the end of it. It also has some awesome characters, a rich worldbuilding, and some powerful moments. I know many people despise it and consider it utter shit. I don't indiscriminately like <i>everything</i> on the show, I share almost none of the opinions of George R.R. Martin, I'm very critical of some of the writing, and I find it a lot of fun and very well done.<br /> <br /> You are not what you eat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:15:15-07:00","id":1213058,"title":"","content":"I regularly consult the Conan RPG books for artifact and character ideas, so yeah. Totally a major exalted influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:53:35-07:00","id":1213079,"title":"","content":"Thank God most writers, creators, etc. throughout the history of the world are offensive to the rabidly PC culture of our day. We\u2019re heading toward some kind of apocalypse where no one can have any genuine belief or opinion that isn\u2019t evaluated and punished by the gestapo of political correctness. Ugh. I have also never read Conan, but now I want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T09:10:05-07:00","id":1213084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1213079#post1213079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank God most writers, creators, etc. throughout the history of the world are offensive to the rabidly PC culture of our day. We\u2019re heading toward some kind of apocalypse where no one can have any genuine belief or opinion that isn\u2019t evaluated and punished by the gestapo of political correctness. Ugh. I have also never read Conan, but now I want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know it\u2019s so frustrating today that we actually have to listen now to things people of color having been saying through all of modern history. It\u2019s a horrible violation of your freedom that people who are negatively impacted by regurgitated cultural stereotypes aren\u2019t being systematically silenced as they used to be. What a tragic injustice.<br /> <br /> Thank god that most of western literary history reuses the same racial and gender tropes over and over and over rather than having the horrible diverse stories that we\u2019re starting to see today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-29-2018, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":24}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:21:34-07:00","id":1213103,"title":"","content":"I mean, it <i>would</i> be nice if people could actually discuss classic genre fiction without being immediately drowned by a stock* back and forth of oh-so-helpful reminders that one doesn't read eighty year old pulp novels for the social commentary and totally-needed disclaimers that that doesn't automatically make them bad books. Like, thanks, I never would have guessed either of those things.<br /> <br /> * Seriously, this thread is giving me such deja vu I'm almost tempted to check for copy-pasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:45:09-07:00","id":1213117,"title":"","content":"Go read Conan if you want! I'd not for a minute suggest that people shouldn't be allowed to read it, or that if people did read it, this then poses pose some kind of insidious risk of Dangerous Thoughts, or is responsible for some kind of political injustice.<br /> <br /> But in context I thought it was worth noting that my experience was Conan seemed explicitly racial in a way that is really quite unusual for Sword &amp; Sorcery of its time - the whole Hyborian Age history Howard gives is really focused on the ascendancy and degeneration of &quot;races&quot; who are in a struggle for survival (ascendancy seeming to be about evolution towards a sort of idealized Northern European type, degeneration often mentioned in terms about &quot;racial&quot; mixing and &quot;purity&quot;); characterization is often explaining characters' traits by their race; civilization makes character and peoples weak. And so on.<br /> <br /> If you think this stuff is all a load of nonsense then it seems to me kind of hard to get around it, and that unfortunately was my personal experience. It's all a lot more prominent in the narrative than something like Tolkein's &quot;Well, the elves do sort of a look a bit like idealized tall, slim Scandinavian folk, and the orcs do speak with working class cockney accents and probably looked a bit like Mongols in Tolkein's mind's eye, and Numenoreans are just better than everyone else... But the books actually have a lot more substance and universal human appeal than that and you can mostly ignore this for the purposes of the plot.&quot;. If you can get around it, then more power to you.<br /> <br /> (I guess this is not a very positive contribution to this thread though, so I'll shurrup now.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:57:39-07:00","id":1213120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1213103#post1213103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it <i>would</i> be nice if people could actually discuss classic genre fiction without being immediately drowned by a stock* back and forth of oh-so-helpful reminders that one doesn't read eighty year old pulp novels for the social commentary and totally-needed disclaimers that that doesn't automatically make them bad books. Like, thanks, I never would have guessed either of those things.<br /> <br /> * Seriously, this thread is giving me such deja vu I'm almost tempted to check for copy-pasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who 100% believes we should be socially critical of and actively discuss these themes, I agree it doesn\u2019t make it a \u201cbad book\u201d and I don\u2019t think most people engaged in said criticism do either. It\u2019s just a strongly present element of the setting that should not be ignored. It\u2019s not about censorship, it\u2019s about critical analysis and engagement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T11:26:15-07:00","id":1213130,"title":"","content":"It's also, as Roswynn put it, old news. To the point that thread derailment is the only thing bringing it up anyway really seems to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T11:50:59-07:00","id":1213138,"title":"","content":"I wonder how many exalted players that became kings had as much of a loyalty problem from the populace as Conan did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:13:42-07:00","id":1213453,"title":"","content":"I think it really depends on your ST, tbh.<br /> <br /> I generally find that most PCs who are Kings have lots of loyalty problems... but that's because the players and STs in our group are often interested in things like power relationships, unrest, class conflict, etc.<br /> If you had a group who were mostly interested in conquering stuff and having lots of exciting pitched battles, I imagine they'd have much more loyal populaces.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:45:56-07:00","id":1213466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1213453#post1213453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it really depends on your ST, tbh.<br /> <br /> I generally find that most PCs who are Kings have lots of loyalty problems... but that's because the players and STs in our group are often interested in things like power relationships, unrest, class conflict, etc.<br /> If you had a group who were mostly interested in conquering stuff and having lots of exciting pitched battles, I imagine they'd have much more loyal populaces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or not - you have to work on that loyalty to get troops, reserves, morale and etc. :P<br /> <br /> And i wouldn't say it was <b>so</b> bad for Conan, as things take for a interesting turn in Hour of Dragon, when a relative of the deposed king manages to retake the Aquilonian throne and comes the time for him to deal with Conan loyalists among other things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-30-2018, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T14:46:56-07:00","id":1213898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game#post1212634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, this isn't news. It's not like the Conan books haven't been referenced throughout the history of the line. Most relevantly there was the third edition statement that the sorcery rewrite was heavily influenced by them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been re-reading some of my Karl Edward Wagner Kane books recently, and the treatment of sorcery in those strikes me as an even better match for Exalted 3e. In <i>Darkness Weaves</i> we see a sorceress using a quickly available spell against enemies (as well as the protagonist countering it at an opportune moment), summon a demonic familiar as a source of knowledge, and go through some explicitly described lengthy steps to prepare a sorcerous working that transmigrates her soul with another's. There are also surviving prehuman antiquities that make use of forgotten occult science beyond the understanding of people in the present day.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T17:08:44-07:00","id":1213971,"title":"","content":"In a bit of a weird twist, Jack Vance's <b>The Dying Earth</b> has some of the most notably Exalted 3e-style sorcery about, including workings and such. I think it's wroth looking into and thinking I think a bit too on the irony that both Exalted 3e and D&amp;D draw on it, but kind of take completely different lessons from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T03:03:02-07:00","id":1215722,"title":"","content":"Right, I see my &quot;political correctness&quot; (I call it &quot;ethics&quot; and &quot;basic decency&quot;) almost choked a couple dudebros. I'm honestly a little surprised, I remembered these forums as less of a shelter for Alt-Reich reactionaries, but we all have our disappointments, big and small.<br /> <br /> What can I say? Conan doesn't exactly make my heart beat faster. It's mostly the story of a walking, white, cis, hetero, male power fantasy with almost no flaws, getting laid with any raven-tressed and ivory-skinned damsel in distress the author cares to lay, barely covered in jewelled lingerie and with the body of a goddess, at his feet. He's not without merit, as a character - he can be interesting, he can be cunning, he can be scared shitless (thank Mithras!), he's not completely invincible. I could do without his chivalrous attitudes and with more intelligent, capable, complex women (actually so, not just <i>described</i> as such).<br /> <br /> Thoth-Amon is interesting as well, I would've liked to read more about him (and his sister, who was just fridged of course). Belit becomes useful - after she's dead. There are some rich and colorful descriptions in the books, and some decent fights - mostly involving weapons, which I'm admittedly a fan of (although if Howard deigned himself to study a little hoplology before writing about actual fights, maybe it would read a bit better), but also wits and will, and some sweet sorcerous imagery.<br /> <br /> There's all the baggage you would expect from a guy who wrote in the '30s. He's not always racist, but Belit is a Shemite and as such dies for her greed (Jewish people and their attachment to money, natch!). Most people of non-white races tend to be treacherous, or foolish. Not always, and not only them, sure, but that's the trend. No homosexuals or similarly non-heteronormative characters in sight, just some homoerotic hints here and there and some evil almost-lesbians... no diversity in general...<br /> <br /> I don't know, I'm not really a fan. Yes, sure, the 30's. Doesn't make it any more palatable.<br /> <br /> Exalted? Exalted has a <i>fuckton</i> of complex female characters, of homosexual relationships, of actually different cultures whithout a clear superior one and &quot;degenerate savages&quot; blah blah blah. There are people with disabilities who can outfight or outsmart anyone in the neighbourhood, there are trans people, there are deeply flawed characters and beautiful plots and characterizations.<br /> <br /> In all honesty I don't play Exalted to recreate crappy pulp from almost a century ago. But hey, you like Conan? Great news, have a blast! Peace out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T04:27:47-07:00","id":1215732,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hoplology&quot; is definitely one of the most interesting new words I've learned in a while. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T05:12:06-07:00","id":1215741,"title":"","content":"It's also an awesome field of study, if you like physical fighting in general (and let's be honest, many of us rpgamers fucking love a good fight - whether it's more realistic or cinematic is immaterial). It's also not too distant from military history, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:05:09-07:00","id":1215770,"title":"","content":"I find it ironic that many champions of ethics and basic decency often step down of their pedestals and engage in the behaviors they so readily and extensively criticize, like branding groups of people they disagree with insulting and dismissive labels.<br /> <br /> Maybe they feel the uncouth masses are not ready to be treated with the ethics and basic decency they talk so much about, and must be treated in the way they treat others, because that is the only way they can understand. <br /> <br /> Yes, that must be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:36:46-07:00","id":1215783,"title":"","content":"...Well, I guess I failed <i>that</i> Topic-Shifting Reply roll after all. -.-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T08:55:28-07:00","id":1215808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1215770#post1215770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it ironic that many champions of ethics and basic decency often step down of their pedestals and engage in the behaviors they so readily and extensively criticize, like branding groups of people they disagree with insulting and dismissive labels.<br /> <br /> Maybe they feel the uncouth masses are not ready to be treated with the ethics and basic decency they talk so much about, and must be treated in the way they treat others, because that is the only way they can understand.<br /> <br /> Yes, that must be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure that you're batting for the team that you think you are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:20:00-07:00","id":1215824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1215770#post1215770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it ironic that many champions of ethics and basic decency often step down of their pedestals and engage in the behaviors they so readily and extensively criticize, like branding groups of people they disagree with insulting and dismissive labels.<br /> <br /> Maybe they feel the uncouth masses are not ready to be treated with the ethics and basic decency they talk so much about, and must be treated in the way they treat others, because that is the only way they can understand.<br /> <br /> Yes, that must be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, look, I don't expect some people to understand absolutely a single flying, landbound or maritime fuck. I just have a little fun. Bye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:33:58-07:00","id":1215829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1215808#post1215808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure that you're batting for the team that you think you are?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not batting for any team. I'm just being a prickish devil's advocate trying to get people to be consistent and try practicing what they preach a little.<br /> <br /> I was raised on family where 90% of the time the men bailed and the women were doing everything. They were professionals, cared for the household, and raised the next generation as best they could. I have gay friends, family members, and believe they should be able to have any legal benefit afforded to anyone, like getting married.<br /> <br /> I am all for female empowerment, LGBTQ+ equality, and that we should be responsible stewards of this planet.<br /> <br /> I also think one can consume, and appreciate, art created sexist, bigoted assholes and not be sexist, bigoted assholes themselves. And not care about it. Specially when said asshole is from decades (centuries, millennia) ago. <br /> <br /> Maybe I have one foot in each side, who would've known. I'm damned to be ostracized by all, not virtuous enough for either side. <br /> <br /> Let me go cry in a corner (not really).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T10:22:50-07:00","id":1215842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1215824#post1215824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, look, I don't expect some people to understand absolutely a single flying, landbound or maritime fuck. I just have a little fun. Bye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I just find it distasteful to imply people associate with Nazism because something as banal as liking Conan and not caring about all the complicated things you feel they should care about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T11:24:09-07:00","id":1215864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1215722#post1215722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, I see my &quot;political correctness&quot; (I call it &quot;ethics&quot; and &quot;basic decency&quot;) almost choked a couple dudebros. I'm honestly a little surprised, I remembered these forums as less of a shelter for Alt-Reich reactionaries, but we all have our disappointments, big and small.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">These forums are hardly a shelter for alt-Reich reactionaries and implying that is utter bullshit. If you want to make personal or group attacks rather than reporting the post you take issue with then this isn't the forum for you. Consider this an official warning, don't do it again. You don't have to agree with someone but you do have to be courteous about your disagreement if you want to keep posting here.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T10:18:51-07:00","id":1218249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1215842#post1215842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I just find it distasteful to imply people associate with Nazism because something as banal as liking Conan and not caring about all the complicated things you feel they should care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, I already said liking Conan isn't badwrongfun and doesn't make you a bad person. Don't twist what I'm saying. I like GoT for chrissakes, who am I to judge?<br /> <br /> I also find people who are afraid of the political correctness apocalypse and who think racism, sexism, homophobia and ableism are cool are patently ridiculous individuals, I don't have to teach them anything, I don't have to educate them in being better people, and I absolutely despise them and don't give a rat's ass if I offend them. If they miraculously change their mind, cool, then we can have a civilized discussion. But I've met this kind of people many many <b>MANY</b> times and no matter your intentions, they just don't wanna change. They love their privilege and will invent ridiculous conspiracies to justify why <i>they</i> and their right to their opinions are the victims, poor babies. I'm sorry, I'm fed up with this shit and I'm not making excuses to <b>ANYONE</b>.<br /> <br /> Have a nice day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T12:24:31-07:00","id":1218294,"title":"","content":"2120 Student: So people a hundred years ago didn't really know much about where their stuff came from huh?<br /> <br /> 2120 Teacher: Oh no, actually most of them either had a very good idea, or just a vague kind of understanding of the whole thing.<br /> <br /> 2120 Student: I don't get it...didn't they have like those huge long debates about morality and ethics and this huge overturn of cultural oppression around then?<br /> <br /> 2120 Teacher: Oh yes, and ironically most of these debates happened on online forums, with everyone involved using devices that were manufactured in unethical and unsustainable ways.<br /> <br /> 2120 Student: But...I don't get it. So they were all monsters then? How could they understand what their culture was doing and even pretend a little bit like any of them were good people? We'd lock those kind of people up today in reformation centers!<br /> <br /> 2120 Teacher: Yes yes, and we'd be quite right to do so, the destruction of our planet and the lives of those others less fortunate for out own convenience is awful. It's not something that we've really come to understand and act on until the last 40 years, quite recently in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> 2120 Student: Was there anybody who lived in the year 2000 that we could consider to be a good person?<br /> <br /> 2120 Teacher: Yes, a few scattered people who lived completely sustainably off their own work, but proportionally almost none of them had an impact on the dominant cultures. Most of them were either poor, isolated, or both.<br /> <br /> 2120 Student: Wow, I don't know if I can ever enjoy anything those people made...At least NOW most of us are doing everything right.<br /> <br /> 2120 Teacher: Yes, at least now we are. I would recommend giving some of their work a second look though, their words and ideals were usually much better than their actual actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T13:20:20-07:00","id":1218305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1212815#post1212815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*This isn't really directed at anyone in specific, but I've seen lots of situations online where someone says, &quot;I really enjoyed X!&quot; and then people say, &quot;Yeah but the guy who made it is a scumbag,&quot; and the original poster ends up feeling like he's being attacked for supporting the actions of the creator.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a similar vein, someone can make an argument that speaks to the truth of a matter even if they're a horrible person.<br /> <br /> You're not required to ignore the fact that they're a horrible person, but it's best to acknowledge the two times a day that a broken clock tells the correct time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T15:26:56-07:00","id":1218348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218294#post1218294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2120 Student: So people a hundred years ago didn't really know much about where their stuff came from huh? [<b><i>snip</i></b>]</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe these 2120 perfectly moral beings should consider they wouldn't be there if there hadn't been actual activists of all stripes in the 2000s trying to change their own internalized behaviors from the ideas they inherited from previous centuries, to think critically, to try to make even a little difference, to fight for their own rights as women, disabled people, LGBTQ individuals, and many other important and historically ostracized and persecuted minorities.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they're just huge dicks and all we're trying to do is worth nothing. But at least we'll have tried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T16:57:11-07:00","id":1218362,"title":"","content":"Nah but the Conan stories are super racist and sexist, and if you\u2019ve got a problem admitting it then you need to reevaluate your priorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T17:15:33-07:00","id":1218365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218348#post1218348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe these 2120 perfectly moral beings should consider they wouldn't be there if there hadn't been actual activists of all stripes in the 2000s trying to change their own internalized behaviors from the ideas they inherited from previous centuries, to think critically, to try to make even a little difference, to fight for their own rights as women, disabled people, LGBTQ individuals, and many other important and historically ostracized and persecuted minorities.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they're just huge dicks and all we're trying to do is worth nothing. But at least we'll have tried.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just trying to point out that if we judge people from the past as though they existed today instead of being partly a product of their environment, then we too must be judged by the fact that at this very moment we are doing many things which will one day be considered abhorant behaviour. .<br /> <br /> It\u2019s sort of like that old question, would you have been a part of Stalin\u2019s horrible communist regime, or a Nazi or a British colonist? That question doesn\u2019t suppose that if you, right now, we\u2019re transported to that place and time would you resist. It supposes if you grew up surrounded in that environment would you have complied? The answer is actually yes, probably. <br /> <br /> Well, it\u2019s either that or Germans/Russians/Brits are just soulless murderers and nobody else is capable of being that.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure you know this though. What you might think is that because you know this you\u2019re immune to it. I\u2019m sure it gives you some defence against it, so it\u2019s good to know, and good to tell other people of. Show them the Milgram experiments and stuff, the banality of evil, but no it doesn\u2019t make you immune.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not even up for debate that the metals in your computer were dug up from the ground and totally screw with the Earth\u2019s mineral cycle. They were produced and shipped with totally unsustainable practices environmentally, and almost certainly worked on by people with abysmal wages and working conditions.<br /> <br /> You haven\u2019t refused to use your computer, you haven\u2019t stopped using fossil fuel based transport, you haven\u2019t stopped purchasing goods from foriegn countries with lax labor laws. Neither have I, clearly.<br /> <br /> People in the future will look at me and you with the same comical irony that we today look at Tomas Jefferson, the slave owner who wrote \u201call men are created equal, with certain, inalienable rights. Among these life, liberty and the persuit of happiness.\u201d Or the fact that Abraham Lincoln was totally a racist, even though he officially ended slavery in America.<br /> <br /> And even THEN I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll think they\u2019ve got it all figured out, only to have people 100 years later shake their heads at all they did wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying don\u2019t fight for LGBTQ rights or anything, of course so it, that\u2019s how we\u2019ll change things. I just hope you realize there\u2019s a thousand other issues that you\u2019re benefitting from, that you\u2019re not bending over backwards and sacrificing to change, and maybe that doesn\u2019t make you a despicable person. And just maybe that means that people who lived a very long time ago in a very different environment weren\u2019t despicable either, in spite of how we might be tempted to view them today. <br /> <br /> Or at the very least, we\u2019re in no position to criticize them for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T17:38:05-07:00","id":1218371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mizzlfoshizzl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218362#post1218362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah but the Conan stories are super racist and sexist, and if you\u2019ve got a problem admitting it then you need to reevaluate your priorities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally no one here has been afraid to admit it, so who do you think you\u2019re talking to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:44:23-07:00","id":1218404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218371#post1218371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> who do you think you\u2019re talking to?</div> </div> </div> </div>PnuemaPilot back on p.1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T23:03:57-07:00","id":1218419,"title":"","content":"People. Look. I didn't want to get involved because gods have I been burned bad enough by that tango, but just a few things off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> A\u00b0 Pretty much everyone agrees that the people of centuries past had some serious issues that have leaked in their writing, issues that we should be mindful of as we read them.<br /> <br /> B\u00b0 Pretty much everyone ALSO agrees that those people weren't willfull monsters knowing of their own evil-ness<br /> <br /> C\u00b0 Pretty much everyone ALSO agrees that A\u00b0 and B\u00b0 don't imply their books SHOULDN'T be read, merely that context remains important when reading them<br /> <br /> ALSO D\u00b0 (BIG ONE): If you want to make points, don't do it like me and not mention people in your messages, because right now, you're wondering if I singled YOU out for one of those four points, and even feel insulted because you don't feel like you resemble that point. So consider, when you'll be replying, that you're going to cause the same reaction if you forget to @ the person you're adressing.<br /> <br /> Also, you want my opinion? Conan: cool action pieces, cool scenario outlines. Themes and motifs? Needs a sensitivity upgrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T00:48:26-07:00","id":1218435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218365#post1218365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was just trying to point out that if we judge people from the past as though they existed today instead of being partly a product of their environment, then we too must be judged by the fact that at this very moment we are doing many things which will one day be considered abhorant behaviour. .<br /> <br /> It\u2019s sort of like that old question, would you have been a part of Stalin\u2019s horrible communist regime, or a Nazi or a British colonist? That question doesn\u2019t suppose that if you, right now, we\u2019re transported to that place and time would you resist. It supposes if you grew up surrounded in that environment would you have complied? The answer is actually yes, probably.<br /> <br /> Well, it\u2019s either that or Germans/Russians/Brits are just soulless murderers and nobody else is capable of being that.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure you know this though. What you might think is that because you know this you\u2019re immune to it. I\u2019m sure it gives you some defence against it, so it\u2019s good to know, and good to tell other people of. Show them the Milgram experiments and stuff, the banality of evil, but no it doesn\u2019t make you immune.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not even up for debate that the metals in your computer were dug up from the ground and totally screw with the Earth\u2019s mineral cycle. They were produced and shipped with totally unsustainable practices environmentally, and almost certainly worked on by people with abysmal wages and working conditions.<br /> <br /> You haven\u2019t refused to use your computer, you haven\u2019t stopped using fossil fuel based transport, you haven\u2019t stopped purchasing goods from foriegn countries with lax labor laws. Neither have I, clearly.<br /> <br /> People in the future will look at me and you with the same comical irony that we today look at Tomas Jefferson, the slave owner who wrote \u201call men are created equal, with certain, inalienable rights. Among these life, liberty and the persuit of happiness.\u201d Or the fact that Abraham Lincoln was totally a racist, even though he officially ended slavery in America.<br /> <br /> And even THEN I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll think they\u2019ve got it all figured out, only to have people 100 years later shake their heads at all they did wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying don\u2019t fight for LGBTQ rights or anything, of course so it, that\u2019s how we\u2019ll change things. I just hope you realize there\u2019s a thousand other issues that you\u2019re benefitting from, that you\u2019re not bending over backwards and sacrificing to change, and maybe that doesn\u2019t make you a despicable person. And just maybe that means that people who lived a very long time ago in a very different environment weren\u2019t despicable either, in spite of how we might be tempted to view them today.<br /> <br /> Or at the very least, we\u2019re in no position to criticize them for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you're right, Howard and Lovecraft were partly a product of their environment. Rudyard Kipling too I guess. That doesn't make some of the stuff they wrote any more palatable to me, though.<br /> <br /> Yes, I probably would've been part of some shitty regime or imperialist society. Hell, I'm part of a capitalist, corrupt society right now, which exploits struggling nations to enrich itself. As you mentioned, the parts in this computer were mined and put together by people who are practically slaves. I feel ashamed of that. The only way is trying to turn the results for good, at least a bit.<br /> <br /> I know I'm not ethically immune. I am a racist, even though I try not to be. I have some residual internalized misogyny, even though I'm a woman. And so on. I don't think you can completely divorce yourself from the toxic ideologies you internalized as a kid, as a teen, that even today you're exposed to a thousand times every day. You fight, but the influences are still there.<br /> <br /> I also don't think we've got it all figured out. Moral and ethics are a product of their time and their society. I never said my ethical approach is perfect. I only said I don't take much pleasure by reading the Conan stories - even though I know Howard's ideas were influenced by the society he lived in, it doesn't make his work more pleasant for me. It doesn't mean I hate everyone who came before - there are a lot of people in history I admire. Not completely, not as in, they can do no wrong - they could and they did, but I still can appreciate their ideas, their genius, their talent, their efforts, what they represent to us today.<br /> <br /> I disagree that we're in no position to criticize people in the past. I mean, we have to be mindful of the proper context. And no, most were not despicable, they were just people, just like us. But they're not unassailable just because they lived in a different time. Everyone makes mistakes, but if we don't recognize them and criticize them how do we grow beyond them? My intent is not to mindlessly bash Howard because he doesn't correspond to some golden standard I can't even attain myself. Hell, the guy probably struggled with depression, so I can empathize. Also, his views towards women partook of elements of feminism, and later in life he became less racist, so even though he's no saint, he certainly wasn't a bad person for his day. Still, if we understand and form an opinion of him and other authors of his time, and other people from earlier decades and centuries, and still other people from later, we'll learn how their thought process developed, how our own views took shape, how &quot;the past&quot; is not a monolithic block of bigots but a complex tapestry of various conflicting ideas. I see that as a desirable goal.<br /> <br /> Don't think I'm unaware of all the myriad injustices I do nothing against or I profit from. I'm not. I care, and deeply. But, like everyone, I need to choose my battles, everyday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T06:01:12-07:00","id":1218491,"title":"","content":"Why is exploiting other countries capitalistic? You think communist and socialist countries don\u2019t exploit other countries?<br /> <br /> Fascism involved government control of industry and suppression of political opposition just like communism and socialism, and fascism is definitely exploitative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-14-2018, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T06:18:19-07:00","id":1218496,"title":"","content":"I said<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, I'm part of a capitalist, corrupt society right now, which exploits struggling nations to enrich itself. </div> </div> </div>Not, &quot;I'm part of a capitalist society <b>which therefore</b> exploits struggling nations&quot;.<br /> <br /> Exploiting other countries isn't capitalistic. You got what I wrote wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T07:15:15-07:00","id":1218519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218249#post1218249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like GoT for chrissakes, who am I to judge?</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with Game of Thrones is less the source material and more the smug faux historical explanations I see for its world building decisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T07:27:15-07:00","id":1218527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218249#post1218249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no, I already said liking Conan isn't badwrongfun and doesn't make you a bad person. Don't twist what I'm saying. I like GoT for chrissakes, who am I to judge?<br /> <br /> I also find people who are afraid of the political correctness apocalypse and who think racism, sexism, homophobia and ableism are cool are patently ridiculous individuals, I don't have to teach them anything, I don't have to educate them in being better people, and I absolutely despise them and don't give a rat's ass if I offend them. If they miraculously change their mind, cool, then we can have a civilized discussion. But I've met this kind of people many many <b>MANY</b> times and no matter your intentions, they just don't wanna change. They love their privilege and will invent ridiculous conspiracies to justify why <i>they</i> and their right to their opinions are the victims, poor babies. I'm sorry, I'm fed up with this shit and I'm not making excuses to <b>ANYONE</b>.<br /> <br /> Have a nice day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then, start on yourself and check your white first worlder privilege.<br /> <br /> You do not have the right to offend anyone you want on this forum.<br /> <br /> Nobody here said any of those things you mentioned are cool, and you trying to imply someone did is dishonest and cowardly.<br /> <br /> Your self-righteouness and lack of thought just expose the fultility of your perceived war and your rants.<br /> <br /> You barely have anything to say, you're screaming. Why do you think you have anything to teach that is worth learning?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T10:09:14-07:00","id":1218598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218519#post1218519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with Game of Thrones is less the source material and more the smug faux historical explanations I see for its world building decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely - that is quite infuriating. Like when a Black person asked George R. R. Martin why European-based fantasy is so white and monocultural and he said, &quot;Because it's mostly been written by white men&quot;. Yes, but Europe did have quite a few PoC back in the related eras (or how more recently <a href=\"https://grrm.livejournal.com/378521.html?thread=19372441#t19372441\" target=\"_blank\">a Black fan asked him for more diversity and he said there will be some PoC characters in Winds of Winter... but not too important</a>) and even then, why, since it's all fantasy, why not making it a more diverse setting?<br /> <br /> Anyways, yes - it looks <i>superficially</i> like Medieval Europe, but for instance in the Middle Ages the lowest thrall could bring their lord before the Justices if they didn't fulfill their obligations. The king had to be good to his dukes or they would depose him, and the earls could do the same with them. You couldn't shoot your crossbow at random servants like Joffrey does without being immediately deposed, or flay people alive as for that, and killing whole cities of people was a surefire way to have a depression. If you were a noble you had many important duties and god forgive you if you didn't attend to them. Of course this all varies in different centuries and nations, but that's the gist of it.<br /> <br /> The treatment of women? I could write a book about this... Martin likes to say &quot;history is written in blood&quot; but rape could be punished with whipping, castration, or death. Noblewomen, for starters, could and did handle farms, manors, castles while their husbands were at war - they needed to heed the men's advice, but also be somewhat decent military commanders if the lands were attacked, manage and supervise hundreds of workers, and also be able to keep their husband's business afloat and possibly prospering - most of all in case they were widowed (Sansa shows some enterprise skill in Season 7, which is good).<br /> <br /> Nuns - nuns could study and work, and in convents they handled everything, from farming, to the treasury, to church services, to teaching young girls. Later on they even acquired a lot of servants. They didn't just walk after you chanting &quot;Shame, shame, shame&quot;. Okay, different religion, sure.<br /> <br /> Middle class women, similarly to noblewomen, had to handle their family's townhouse and help with their husband's business, or practice their own different job. Usually no job was forbidden to them. They became apprentices and learned the jobs they wanted to practice - barbers, apothecaries, armorers, shipwrights, masons, carpenters, brewers... they were fewer than men, and weren't allowed to become masters, but they existed. The silk industry was practically all women, even in positions of authority, and they had a lot of power as an organization. Not to mention midwives - forget maesters - they were well-paid, swore oaths, were compensated by the city in the case of a mother too poor to afford their services, had apprentices, distributed public welfare, and acted as backup medical assistants whenever needed. In some cities women could actually study medicine.<br /> <br /> Women without particular skills as craftsfolks could sell food in the streets (like fish - because it was easy to catch, plentiful, and good for days of religious fasting - , or even, admittedly, clams with lemon juice, like Arya does in Braavos). They often became servants, and sometimes nurses or prostitutes. They actually didn't have a lot of nice prospects, that's true.<br /> <br /> Peasant women helped men in all the labor at the farm. They probably worked more than their husbands, considering they had to take care of the kids and spin, spin, always spin textiles for the lord. Some did <i>not</i> marry - they stayed with their families, or they became servants at another farm, or at the manor, becoming maids, sheperds, anything, doing work exactly like any man - or they could travel from town to town and if they managed to stay away from serfdom for a year and a day they were free.<br /> <br /> It's okay if women in GoT are universally oppressed, it's unpleasant, but it can propel some interesting narratives... but let's not say the reason lies in any interest in realism or verisimilitude.<br /> <br /> People also had soap and a sort of toothpaste, so their teeth weren't all rotten (that's okay) and they didn't walk around caked with filth (why are people in fantasy always caked with filth?).<br /> <br /> Also, Arabic culture was a central and very important presence in Europe - at the court of kings, in universities, in the way it influenced poetry, philosophy, trade, science... PoC weren't confined to another continent an ocean away, all slavers and slaves and assassins and exotic eunuch soldiers.<br /> <br /> Also, where are the wall decorations and colors, where are the graffiti? Why is everything so brown and grey and dead, is Dorne the only decent place to live in? Since at least Classical Greece times, people have always painted their architecture - the Middle Ages were no exception.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I too am okay with the narrative in GoT (up to a certain point - really, too many gratuitous rapes and too few PoC... to start with) - but no, it doesn't resemble the Middle Ages much. It just doesn't. If Martin, or the producers and writers, want to find any trace of legitimacy in their work, they will have to look elsewhere - this is Hollywood Middle Ages, or a mix of tropes and clich\u00e8s from a disparate amount of different cultures and epochs. You can't build a setting like this and claim you're doing it to make it feel realistic, to ground it in real world history - go study real world history first, and study it well. Or, alternately, don't go with that explanation - just say you wanted a gritty setting and you only took the worst aspects from various actual sociopolitical realities, at most.<br /> <br /> Jeez.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T10:39:39-07:00","id":1218608,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2746_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2746\" data-vbnamecard=\"2746\">TGUEIROS</a> <br /> <br /> Ooh, brutal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T12:57:15-07:00","id":1218658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218598#post1218598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, I too am okay with the narrative in GoT (up to a certain point - really, too many gratuitous rapes and too few PoC... to start with) - but no, it doesn't resemble the Middle Ages much. It just doesn't. If Martin, or the producers and writers, want to find any trace of legitimacy in their work, they will have to look elsewhere - this is Hollywood Middle Ages, or a mix of tropes and clich\u00e8s from a disparate amount of different cultures and epochs. You can't build a setting like this and claim you're doing it to make it feel realistic, to ground it in real world history - go study real world history first, and study it well. Or, alternately, don't go with that explanation - just say you wanted a gritty setting and you only took the worst aspects from various actual sociopolitical realities, at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. A Song of Fire and Ice isn't anywhere near as clever as people like to pretend it is. A lot of the grittiness in the world only serves to paint our heroes with one colour and our villains with another.<br /> <br /> -The bedding ceremony exists in the form that it does so Ned Stark and Tyrion Lannister get to be gentlemen by refusing.<br /> -Primae Noctis was a thing in Westeros so Roose Bolton could highlight how evil he is.<br /> -Joffery Lannister needed to be an evil little shit to absolve Ned of the fact he basically put Cersei' children on Stannis' hit list.<br /> -Rape and accepting it is basically a shorthand for &quot;this person is evil&quot; its not a major part of Greyjoy and Dothraki culture dehumanising their enemies because apparently Daenerys can just tell them to stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T15:39:15-07:00","id":1218708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218658#post1218658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Rape and accepting it is basically a shorthand for &amp;quot;this person is evil&amp;quot; its not a major part of Greyjoy and Dothraki culture dehumanising their enemies because apparently Daenerys can just tell them to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair on this one, she <i>is</i> a Zenith. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T16:18:37-07:00","id":1218717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218708#post1218708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair on this one, she <i>is</i> a Zenith. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Her arc for multiple seasons was establishing that she couldn't just go &quot;SLAVERY IS OVER!&quot; and sparked that whole confrontation with the League of Shadows ...I know they're not called that but my mother insisted on connecting the Meereen subplot to the Dark Knight Rises and her version of events has kind of pushed the actual one out of my head slightly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T16:27:11-07:00","id":1218721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218708#post1218708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair on this one, she <i>is</i> a Zenith. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's not how Zeniths work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T16:39:51-07:00","id":1218727,"title":"","content":"One minor point that might be interesting to people:<br /> <br /> Weird Tales, the magazine many Conan stories were published in the first time paid more to the writer who wrote a story that went with the cover illustration.<br /> <br /> WT also found that covers with sexy images sold more.<br /> <br /> Several Conan stories were altered to fit in the sexy cover scene because Howard needed the money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T21:42:08-07:00","id":1218802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218658#post1218658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. A Song of Fire and Ice isn't anywhere near as clever as people like to pretend it is. A lot of the grittiness in the world only serves to paint our heroes with one colour and our villains with another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. And GoT isn't clever at all - many people have compared it to a soap opera. Also, all the deconstruction in previous seasons - a honorable protagonist been killed off, a group of knights sworn to protect the king who are essentially a band of glorified thugs, a brotherhood of rangers who takes its members from all manners of criminals - all of it is coming down to &quot;Prophesied king and queen of legend solve everybody's problems and clash against the evil armies of the undead&quot;. I hope they don't go through with this, but with only one season remaining I wouldn't be surprised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218658#post1218658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The bedding ceremony exists in the form that it does so Ned Stark and Tyrion Lannister get to be gentlemen by refusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, being a gentleman, greatest aspiration of white male protagonists everywhere - reminds me of how <a href=\"https://io9.gizmodo.com/5959794/the-firefly-episode-were-really-glad-joss-whedon-didnt-get-to-make\" target=\"_blank\">Joss Whedon wanted to have Inara Serra raped by a whole ship of Reavers so that Mal could be all gentlemanly and stop slut-shaming her</a>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218658#post1218658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Primae Noctis was a thing in Westeros so Roose Bolton could highlight how evil he is.<br /> -Joffery Lannister needed to be an evil little shit to absolve Ned of the fact he basically put Cersei' children on Stannis' hit list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I never thought about it in these terms, but it's true! Although I like how Tommen and Myrcella are actually very good, decent kids.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218658#post1218658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Rape and accepting it is basically a shorthand for &quot;this person is evil&quot; its not a major part of Greyjoy and Dothraki culture dehumanising their enemies because apparently Daenerys can just tell them to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course Dany is the great white savior who will deliver the benighted masses of PoC from their evil ways thanks to her outstanding moral values... Also the Dothraki's utter cruelty would be almost comical if it didn't involve <i>raping hundreds of women in the streets</i>... *sigh*.<br /> <br /> I really like some parts of the show, but others make me want to burn the books in a fire and call it quits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T21:50:19-07:00","id":1218803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218727#post1218727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One minor point that might be interesting to people:<br /> <br /> Weird Tales, the magazine many Conan stories were published in the first time paid more to the writer who wrote a story that went with the cover illustration.<br /> <br /> WT also found that covers with sexy images sold more.<br /> <br /> Several Conan stories were altered to fit in the sexy cover scene because Howard needed the money.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I was reading something similar - essentially WT wanted a sex scene in many stories, but Howard didn't like it, nor many other pulp tropes, and would try to subvert them. He was especially happy with one particular story (Beyond the Black River) precisely because there was no sex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T01:04:42-07:00","id":1218825,"title":"","content":"Hmm... George R R Martin. Well, he's is not a historical or pseudo-historical novelist. He's no Guy Gavriel Kay. That is, he lacks a huge historical background (more so than Exalted strives for and Geoff Grabowski had, on the whole) and has a taste for the lurid (again more so than Exalted, though there's perhaps more of that kind of thing in the dna of how the Realm is written and so on than a complete contrast would imply). He's kind of doing the best he could.<br /> <br /> He also doesn't write pseudo-historical novels (ala GGK) - it's sort of hard to fault Westeros for not replicating European interactions with the rest of the world or their norms when it's a very differentiated place with a different history (Westeros is really governed as some kind of continent sized mega empire that possibly has more parallels to a medieval China, which experienced few interstate conflicts and much more extreme civil wars in absolute scale.)<br /> <br /> He was writing back in '91, and regards himself as a Progressive, so I'd guess if he'd written today, and lacked any burden to make his writing consistent with what went before, he'd have rebalanced with some aspects that made Better Stuff - Essos would not be perhaps the most Orientalist thing ever committed to fantasy fiction. (Some could have for the worse, with various 21st century Progressive myths that no one would have believed back in the Good Old Days incorporated, but I suspect that you need a degree of ignorance and bias to really believe some of those that he just wouldn't have.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T02:44:55-07:00","id":1218843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218825#post1218825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... George R R Martin. Well, he's is not a historical or pseudo-historical novelist.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people really do treat him as such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it's sort of hard to fault Westeros for not replicating European interactions with the rest of the world or their norms when it's a very differentiated place with a different history (Westeros is really governed as some kind of continent sized mega empire that possibly has more parallels to a medieval China, which experienced few interstate conflicts and much more extreme civil wars in absolute scale.)</div> </div> </div> </div> It also has irregular winters that can last for years. If I was a noble in Westeros a summer home overseas would be a really high priority.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T03:38:55-07:00","id":1218853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218708#post1218708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair on this one, she <i>is</i> a Zenith. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking something similar when I was binge-watching the series some months ago, but not for that reason. You know the special relationship she has with her dragons? That looks like a bunch of charms from Survival. They obey her (well, more or less...), she has a great empathy for them, she effectively uses them almost as an extension of herself. Of course that's because she's their &quot;mother&quot;, tied to them via sorcerous means no one fully understands - she's a Targaryen, she was the first living being they saw (a bit like imprinting?), she burnt Mirri Maz Duur while her spell was still fresh and entered the pyre with the eggs... - but if she were an Exalt the same results could be achieved through Survival charms, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T10:37:36-07:00","id":1218959,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in Exalted terms Daenerys is extremely heavy into Presence, Survival, and Integrity in that order... And light on just about everything else, hence why she leaves most of the Bureaucracy and Socialize to her assorted Allies and Retainers with rather mixed results.<br /> <br /> As for the Great White Savior thing, that was actually just an unfortunate accident of logistics; Slaver's Bay and the Free Cities are all extremely cosmopolitan in the books but when you're casting extras you have to make do with whoever's in the area and they filmed most of those scenes in Morocco.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T14:03:34-07:00","id":1219050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218959#post1218959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, in Exalted terms Daenerys is extremely heavy into Presence, Survival, and Integrity in that order... And light on just about everything else, hence why she leaves most of the Bureaucracy and Socialize to her assorted Allies and Retainers with rather mixed results.<br /> <br /> As for the Great White Savior thing, that was actually just an unfortunate accident of logistics; Slaver's Bay and the Free Cities are all extremely cosmopolitan in the books but when you're casting extras you have to make do with whoever's in the area and they filmed most of those scenes in Morocco.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the choice of skills. I think she also has decent Stamina and related charms, I've seen her tough it out quite a lot both in the books and in the show.<br /> <br /> It's been a long time since I read the books, I didn't remember that area of Essos to be so cosmopolitan... but that's certainly better than how it was handled on screen. Even though the extras were necessarily Arab-Berbers, it strikes me that they used a lot of PoC cast as slavers, ex-slaves, Unsullied and so on, while the local head of the Cult of R'llhor (sp?) was Rachel Weisz (I love her, but she's as white as a lily) and of course Daario, who was a PoC in the book, is, again, lily-white in the show.<br /> <br /> But that's a tangent.<br /> <br /> More navel-gazing:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It seems to me that sometimes, when you really like something, its flaws hit you the hardest - I was watching the 1st season of Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt and loving it, and then... racial joke after racial joke, so cringey... I've stopped because it had reached a disturbing level for my tastes.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T14:05:25-07:00","id":1219052,"title":"","content":"For me, the issue with GoT in both book and show form is how deus ex machina and the idiot ball always seem to favor the worst people in the story. By the fourth book or so its just to point of 'oh look, things just happen to go in the villain's favor and the more reasonable character took the stupidest option again.' This ends up turning into a complete sense of apathy regarding the entire setting. After all, if the worst people in the world are going to get a deus ex machina to save them from their own stupidity again, why should I care what happens?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1583-the-insaniac","user":"The Insaniac","date":". 05-15-2018, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1583-the-insaniac","name":"The Insaniac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T14:41:34-07:00","id":1219070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>it's sort of hard to fault Westeros for not replicating European interactions with the rest of the world or their norms when it's a very differentiated place with a different history (Westeros is really governed as some kind of continent sized mega empire that possibly has more parallels to a medieval China, which experienced few interstate conflicts and much more extreme civil wars in absolute scale.)</i> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218843#post1218843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also has irregular winters that can last for years. If I was a noble in Westeros a summer home overseas would be a really high priority.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218598#post1218598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like when a Black person asked George R. R. Martin why European-based fantasy is so white and monocultural and he said, &quot;Because it's mostly been written by white men&quot;. Yes, but Europe did have quite a few PoC back in the related eras (or how more recently <a href=\"https://grrm.livejournal.com/378521.html?thread=19372441#t19372441\" target=\"_blank\">a Black fan asked him for more diversity and he said there will be some PoC characters in Winds of Winter... but not too important</a>) and even then, why, since it's all fantasy, why not making it a more diverse setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I might have misread, but I think these lines of thought tie together?<br /> <br /> <b>I always find it useful to ask the reverse question. </b>The question - &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>why not make it a more diverse setting</i></span>?&quot; demands the reverse - &quot;<i><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">why <b>should </b>it be a more diverse setting</span></i>?&quot;<ul><li><b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Is it fair? </span> Is diversity demanded elsewhere?<br /> </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Where are the voices clamoring for &quot;Hindi&quot; and &quot;Anglo-American&quot; representation in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telenovela\" target=\"_blank\">Telenovelas</a>?<br /> <br /> Where were the voices arguing that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romance_of_the_Three_Kingdoms_(TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">Romance of the Three Kingdoms</a> needed to feature a couple token non-East-Asian characters? Why is it so China-centric?<br /> <br /> When we did a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Brother/Sister_Plays\" target=\"_blank\">Yoruba-inspired play</a> a few years back - where were the voices asking the playwright to feature Huitzilopochtli as a guest-star?<br /> <br /> Should future renditions of Chinese epics with the Monkey King feature Greek satyrs for diversity?<br /> <br /> In fact, when Japan produced <i>Evangelion</i> - they didn't make it <i>great</i> by &quot;diversifying&quot; it with Buddhas or Shinto spirits - instead, they doubled-down on Judeo-Christian esoterica. Not just Christian, they make abundant references to the Old Testament, to the Midrash, Kabbalah and a host of authentic symbols that a lot of Christians aren't familiar with. Doing one thing &quot;really well&quot; produced a better work than &quot;mythology soup&quot; would ever have. <b>And if the</b> Japanese creators were willing to do a Judeo-Christian setting justice (by keeping it <i>authentic </i>within itself) - why is should an American creator be held to a different standard?</div></div> </div> </div></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Is it necessary?</span> <b>Is diversity <i>demanded </i>in art?</b></b><ul><li><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">What right do &quot;fans&quot; have to make claims or demands of an artist? At what point are they obligated to do something they're not inspired to do?<ul><li>Do I get to chastise Keegan &amp; Peele for not having more Hispanic jokes (or better yet, for the caricatures they use)? (Disclaimer: I actually love their humor.)</li> <li>Eminem is a great rapper - I'm a fan - so can I demand he rap in Spanish so as to be more inclusive? Can I impugn on his reputation until he does so?</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#0000ff\">Is it welcome? </span>What reaction would the artist face?</b><ul><li><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If Martin <b>did</b> comply - <span style=\"color:#0000ff\"><b>i</b></span>Inevitably there will be people who would argue that George Martin is &quot;culturally appropriating&quot; non-white peoples to enrich his setting - or they'll claim the characters &quot;weren't important enough&quot; or &quot;bad caricatures&quot; or &quot;reinforce negative stereotypes&quot;. <br /> <br /> Is it not a bit cruel to demand someone do something that they will inevitably be chastised for? Sure - it's nice to think &quot;of the fans seeking representation&quot; - but the artist <i>also</i> is a human being and perhaps he rather not dip his toes into areas of contention.<ul><li>To his credit, I think Dorne and Oberyn Martell were <i>great</i> - but then settings like Warhammer fantasy are so Nord-centric, it feels like the psuedo-Southern-Europeans are reduced to an incompetent footnote and the &quot;Roman Empire&quot; was a Nordic invention. <br /> <br /> <b>My point being</b> that <i>even </i><i>with</i> Europeans creating <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Expy\" target=\"_blank\">expy</a>s of other Europeans, there is ample room for intentional - or unintentional - insult. Is it not a sufficient miracle that an Irish-Italian American writer from Jersey created such an entertaining show - without clamoring for him to include people he might know little about?</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Is it well-aimed? </b></span><b>Is this the best way to diversify?</b><ul><li><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Why should George R.R. Martin be held liable for providing diversity - why not pursue diverse voices?<ul><li>I don't go to Justin Bieber or Beyonce for Spanish songs - I go to <i>Spanish artists</i>. I might <i>appreciate</i> their cross-over gestures (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JWESLtAKKlU\" target=\"_blank\">Pharell featuring on J.Balvin's song is dope</a>) - but I don't <i>expect</i> it from any of them. I don't want some &quot;white guy&quot; pandering to Hispanics - I'll watch new channels like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCeB0K8AL2mCJhrBdCeD2BgA\" target=\"_blank\">FLAMA</a> or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCaemYNcQbzuQKJu6BnxgmxA\" target=\"_blank\">Mit\u00fa</a>. <b>If we want</b> diverse work, we should <i>write it ourselves </i>and <i>produce it ourselves</i> and get it out there.</li> <li>Moreover, if I want more diversity - why not ask it of Jordan Peele (who has new projects in the works)? Or Tarel Alvin McCraney (playwright, screenwriter, MacArthur Genius Award winner, <i>Moonlight</i> is the tip of the iceberg of his work); my friends are hyped for Boots Riley's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=enH3xA4mYcY\" target=\"_blank\">Sorry to Bother You</a>. <i>And those are the Americans! </i>If you specifically want to see more North &amp; West African inspired works - find people there. Do more <i>Black Panther</i> films (it certainly sold well enough).<br /> <br /> <i>Why are &quot;white guys&quot; responsible for writing creative works for other people? </i>Do the Chinese and Hindi sit around, waiting for Hollywood to include them in their scripts before Bollywood starts hiring?</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div></li> </ul></li> </ul>So no, Westeros does <b>not</b> need to lampshade every European interaction. It's a <i>fantasy setting</i>. Multi-year winters are more inspired by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fimbulwinter\" target=\"_blank\">Fimbulwinter</a> than by X, Y, Z, historical event. We should be thinking &quot;grim dark Nordic people seeing death and desperation&quot; not &quot;this show is making commentary on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Frost_of_1709\" target=\"_blank\">the Great Frost of 1709</a>&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People also had soap and a sort of toothpaste, so their teeth weren't all rotten (that's okay) and they didn't walk around caked with filth (why are people in fantasy always caked with filth?). </div> </div> </div>Piss and baths!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>re: Teeth</b><br /> Actually, even back to Roman times, Iberians were known to have clean teeth - <i>because they washed their mouths with piss</i>. You didn't have chalk-and-soap mixes until the 1850s+.<br /> <br /> <b>re: Bathing</b><br /> The Romans wrote about Celtic hair-washing - <b>but</b> the mixture in the water they used <i>thickened</i> their hair such that the Romans claimed it made the Celts look like satyrs. Combine this with Iberian-Celtic piss-gargling and you have hairy, pearly-teethed barbarian satyrs as models of &quot;cleanliness&quot;. Now make them <b>Western </b>Iberian Celts and you can add &quot;mark their property with decapitated heads so as to warn away enemies&quot; to the list of &quot;cleanliness&quot; practices. Or go with tribes who worshiped <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toutatis\" target=\"_blank\">Toutatis</a> - whose form of ritual sacrifice was <i>drowning</i> - and debate how often you want to take a plunge.<br /> <br /> Anglo-Saxons at one point thought Vikings were &quot;overly concerned with cleanliness&quot; since they bathed <b>once a week</b>.<br /> <br /> Saints - I love Saints! St. Fintan of Clonenagh was so austere, his monastery didn't even own a cow for milk - the other monks had to beg for permission to spruce up their diet (and St. Fintan permitted it, but he refused to indulge himself). He also <b>bathed once a year</b> - just before Easter - for 24 years.<br /> <br /> And then you have <b>odd rules</b> for bathing - like the healing baths at <a href=\"https://bathlocator.com/2016/09/26/history-thermal-baths-part-ii-middle-age/\" target=\"_blank\">Burmi</a> (Italy, near Switzerland's border). Rules included &quot;no bathing if you had sex recently&quot; (keep that sexy bump-and-grind smell on you), &quot;no bathing if you ate recently&quot; - you &quot;cant pour water on your head unless clean-shaven&quot;. Oh, and if you bathe for<b> 15 days for 1 hour each</b>, the &quot;health benefits&quot; <b>last 6 months</b>. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Arabic culture was a central and very important presence in Europe - at the court of kings, in universities, in the way it influenced poetry, philosophy, trade, science... PoC weren't confined to another continent an ocean away, all slavers and slaves and assassins and exotic eunuch soldiers. </div> </div> </div>Depiction of all peoples - regardless of skin tone - <i>should be equal</i>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yes, Arab culture was <i>important</i> - and some of it positive (they preserved a lot of Greco-Roman writings that had been lost during wars/fires) - but the pretext for their appearance was <i>expansion by conquest in pursuit of slaves </i>(because of religious prohibitions against enslaving their co-religionists - they had to constantly seek out more heathens). <br /> <br /> They don't get to escape that legacy any more than the Nords escape <i>being Vikings who rape and pillage</i> (despite that the whole feudal system was a synthesis between Roman law and Nordic culture). <br /> <br /> Influencing &quot;poetry, philosophy, trade, science&quot; doesn't redeem much. When the Portuguese monarchs fled Napoleon, they fled to S\u00e3o Paulo - and brought university, craftsmen, architects and your &quot;poetry, philosophy, trade, science&quot;. The Portuguese monarchs presence in Brazil is credited to the stability of the country and the peaceful development of the country. Do the Portuguese get a &quot;free pass&quot; to no longer be depicted as Conquistadors?<br /> <br /> <b>And I'm <i>fond</i> of Arabic.</b> There are Arabic-specific expressions/meanings/idioms like there are Spanish-specific ones - neither of which translate to English. Double-meanings that add-up a hundred ways to then point to cultural differences. Different ways we deal with ambiguity (a virtue in Spanish but a flaw in English). I'm extremely fond of <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/7f/61/b8/7f61b8dfc3c65438a7bcb3735de21d58.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Nizar Qabbani</a>, <a href=\"https://stepcdn.com/assets/2017-08/10/10/cvid9/coffee-png-700x.png\" target=\"_blank\">Mahmoud Darwish</a>, <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/9a/59/a6/9a59a65e37bd3c6d1517366a3d720b58.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Mohammed Abrar Ahmed</a> - and I'm dying to find that <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=1f_cCQAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PA174&amp;lpg=PA174&amp;dq=arabic+whitman+&amp;quot;to+a+stranger&amp;quot;&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=agWX3bu3fo&amp;sig=QfM4dXY7HuB3no46VTUfXYDLn5c&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwig_IGarYjbAhWS2VMKHSoNDu4Q6AEILjAB#v=onepage&amp;q=arabic%20whitman%20&amp;quot;to%20a%20stranger&amp;quot;&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">Iraqi translation</a> of Walt Whitman's <i>Leaves of Grass </i>(I'm familiar with the English, obviously - but the Arabic version implies new meanings because it's the nature of translation that you can't avoid such).<br /> <br /> But my admiration (for the positives) does not result in blindness (for the negative). <br /> <br /> Qabbani's poetry <b><i>wouldn't exist without the negatives</i></b> - he was inspired by his sisters' arranged marriage (and subsequent suicide) as well as the deaths of two wives (different time periods, different wars). He criticized his own culture - and was <b>lauded </b>for it (it was an Omani professor who pointed me to this Syrian with praise). <br /> <br /> The Iraqi version of Leaves of Grass takes &quot;To a Stranger&quot; but <b>adds</b> overtones of exile, culture, migration - and the author/translator was exiled 2 years later. It was the <b>negatives</b> of his culture that helped inspire the translation into a new work.<br /> <br /> In other words, the desire to &quot;only showcase the positive&quot; can be ill-informed. Without the negatives, many of the positives <i>wouldn't exist</i>. It reduces people to &quot;happy, friendly, perfect&quot; little caricatures divorced from reality (and worse yet - when people <b>believe</b> those caricatures, they inevitably demonize the opposition).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the Dothraki's utter cruelty would be almost comical if it didn't involve <i>raping hundreds of women in the streets</i>... *sigh*. </div> </div> </div>You mean like the Mongols who - in addition to horse-riding tribes that bragged about mass genocide - they also spread their seed to include 8% of <i>all </i>men living in the former Mongol Empire? That's <i>everyone</i> from China to Iran - up to Turkey and Russia - and back across Kazakhstan to Mongolia. They did a few nice things for women on the side.<br /> <br /> We either &quot;accept everyone&quot; (good and bad) or &quot;condemn everyone&quot; (good and bad).<br /> No one gets a Disney-approved rendition in history just because they're non-European.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, where are the wall decorations and colors, where are the graffiti? Why is everything so brown and grey and dead, is Dorne the only decent place to live in? Since at least Classical Greece times, people have always painted their architecture - the Middle Ages were no exception. </div> </div> </div>Would the difference be building materials and culture?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Greeks and Romans painted their stuff - but I thought Anglo-Saxons <b>didn't </b>- with most castles/forts being plastered white (at best) and any luxuries reserved for indoors. Different climates in Northern vs Southern Europe shaped the architecture and decor.<br /> <br /> There are other cultures (outside Europe) who were less keen on paint and more keen on sculpture or architecture.<br /> <br /> Dorne's inspirations (I think) are Iberian/Berber/Arab. By Islam prohibiting paintings &amp; sculpture, the art was &quot;funneled&quot; into calligraphy, geometry and patterns - so you end up with architecture that better resists the elements (using different stone or cuts instead of paint - which in turn resists sun bleaching). <br /> <br /> IE, Europeans <i>permitting</i> paint resulted in (a) vulnerable public works that bleached over time and (b) an expensive method of decoration considered frivolous in more austere times. Arabs <i>prohibiting</i> forms of art resulted in (a) trying to create beauty without paint, leading to geometry &amp; architecture that endures longer.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> just say you wanted a gritty setting and you only took the worst aspects from various actual sociopolitical realities, at most. </div> </div> </div>Does this have to be spelled out? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I never watched Game of Thrones expecting <i>historical accuracy.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218802#post1218802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, being a gentleman, greatest aspiration of white male protagonists everywhere - reminds me of how [URL=&quot;https://io9.gizmodo.com/5959794/the-firefly-episode-were-really-glad-joss-whedon-didnt-get-to-make&quot;]Joss Whedon wanted to have Inara Serra raped by a whole ship of Reavers so that Mal could be all gentlemanly and stop slut-shaming her</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is the worst interpretation the defacto one?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Why is the possibility of Mal having some (awful) realization and character growth as a result of a friend's tragedy so offensive? Isn't it important to (clumsily) convey &quot;you don't know what other people have gone through - so don't judge&quot; than to chastise them for daring to ponder a script to have the conversation? <br /> <br /> Victims have stories - but the people around those victims <b>also</b> have stories. How do you expect to create allies if you condemn the mere contemplation of such dialogue?<br /> <br /> Take for instance Gamora in the comics - and when she was <a href=\"https://img.4plebs.org/boards/tv/image/1524/76/1524765730777.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">raped and beaten</a>. The comics don't glorify the rape - and Thanos is stereotypically the &quot;protector who shows up to the rescue&quot;.... <i>but that's the point</i>.<ul><li>That even the most genocidal, callous warlord finds it <i>reprehensible</i>.</li> <li>And that even having &quot;all the power&quot; won't protect your loved ones (so in a sense, if you're a dick, fear karma and beware the influences you bring around your family).</li> <li>That being overly protective leaves your children vulnerable - you need to give girls liberty to experience things.</li> <li>That disobeying your parents warnings can lead you to horrors at times (if you think a conservative family member is &quot;bad&quot; - take a step to consider what their prohibitions might be trying to protect you from)..</li> </ul>It's not about glorifying Thanos. It's not about the &quot;aspiration of male protagonists&quot;. It's about a shitty relationship with shitty situations and people having the &quot;oh fuck&quot; moment. <b>And if a guy writes that script</b>, can we blame them? <i>At least they're trying</i> to engage the topic from whatever perspective they have (as opposed to moving on to something more self-absorbed).<br /> <br /> <br /> You want to disregard male characters who strive to be &quot;gentlemen&quot;? That's fine. But what are you elevating in it's place then? Because these choices don't exist in a vacuum. <br /> <br /> If the characters who <i>show concern</i> for females (even if they're clumsy, misguided or wrong) deserve nothing but ridicule - then why would anyone admire them? <br /> <br /> And what prevents the ugly logic of &quot;well, if the good guys are heckled - who gives a fuck?&quot; There are <i>plenty</i> of men who are <b>glad</b> for women who don't desire gentlemen. I'm not even talking about rapists - just really jaded people who <i>love</i> really jaded women because they can get their dicks wet - and if a girl makes overtures wanting <i>more</i>, they can shrug and go &quot;you knew the terms - I never promised more than dick&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>It creates a &quot;new normal&quot;</b> where since &quot;trying to be decent&quot; gets you heckled, <b>the safest</b> bet is to promise to be an asshole. You need to show compassion to receive compassion (and mocking tropes that try to glorify compassion is the quickest way to mock compassion itself).<br /> <hr /><br /> Or by analogy, yes - if you had a film where a &quot;British people show up to save East Asia!&quot; - I might smirk and roll my eyes. And I'll engage in a fun convo when appropriate. But I'm <b>not</b> going to demonize the <i>mere concept</i> of <i>wanting to save people</i> -- unless I'm ready to later go &quot;oh gee, why are the British disinterested in East Asia?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Better </b>a clumsy - but well-intentioned - ally than a disinterested, jaded or callous stranger.<br /> <br /> <b>Incidentally</b>, this goes hand-in-hand with the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2014/dec/25/where-did-indian-ocean-tsunami-aid-money-go\" target=\"_blank\">2004 Tsunami relief efforts</a>. $6.25 billion was raised - the <b>highest</b> single-donors being the British (approximately $529 million - or 8%). The European commission, the US, Germany, Canada, Norway all <i>showed up to donate and save people</i>.<br /> <br /> And I remember it because Ong-Bak was used to promote a lot - Tony Jaa toured to perform stunts and raise awareness. Tons of &quot;dumb macho jock&quot; customers who like action films &amp; kung-fu - showed up in droves to buy Indonesian and Thai films as part of the fundraising effort. <b>Thank </b>(whatever god you believe in) that they aspired to be <i>good men </i>and valued <i>brotherhood</i> and <i>compassion </i>and weren't rotted away by the cynicism people preach. They didn't need to know <i>shit</i> about East Asia - their <i>intentions</i> were enough.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218959#post1218959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Great White Savior thing, that was actually just an unfortunate accident of logistics; Slaver's Bay and the Free Cities are all extremely cosmopolitan in the books but when you're casting extras you have to make do with whoever's in the area and they filmed most of those scenes in Morocco.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are all kinds of appropriate/odd coincidences (or maybe they're deliberate choices).<br /> <br /> I'm not going to dispute the &quot;Great White Savior&quot; thing if that's what folks latch on to.<br /> <br /> But Morocco and Mauritania and other Moorish/Berber territories still have slavery today, buried as cultural practices and traditions. So filming there is appropriate.<br /> <br /> And when they raided Iberia? They favored Basque women for being especially &quot;white&quot; - taking them as slaves/concubines. The practice was so popular it <i>recolored their bloodlines</i>, and today - despite that the Beydan and <a href=\"http://minorityrights.org/minorities/haratin/\" target=\"_blank\">Haratines</a> are <b>both</b> descended from &quot;black&quot; African roots (and in Spanish we'd call both <i>Morenos</i>) - the Beydan have Berber and Basque blood as well. So the Beydan are considered &quot;white&quot; and the Haratines are &quot;black&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>And then</b> the Basque - coincidentally - still have their reputation as &quot;witches&quot; (neither Christianity, Islam nor the Inquisition could fully convert them).<br /> <br /> So I see Daenerys as a juxtaposition of a Basque woman (&quot;magical bloodlines who look different&quot; + &quot;white slave-concubine&quot;) and her skin-tone means nothing more than &quot;she's foreign&quot;. Meanwhile, Mirri Maz Duur - the witch who results in the child being stillborn? She's a <b>Maegi </b>(female blood magic practitioner)? Well in Galicia, the witches are called <a href=\"https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meiga\" target=\"_blank\">Meiga</a> (different from a Bruxa / Bruja = pronounced &quot;Brew-Ha&quot;). Although they reached the region, the Moors abandoned Galicia because the people &quot;lived in a mountain full of monsters&quot; and &quot;their only sport is violence&quot; and they'd make terrible slaves.<br /> <br /> So the Dothraki are essentially Mongols with a pinch of Moors.<br /> The Maegi are psuedo-Galicians with blood-oaths (willing to die for revenge).<br /> And Daenerys is a psuedo-Basque victim-turned-leader with ancestral magic.<br /> (Tangent: And Dorne is Moorish Spain with a splash of Welsh/Cornish. Crazy how exotic one real-world peninsula can be.)<br /> <br /> And Slaver's Bay <b>is</b> cosmopolitan - but non-locals can't tell the difference between group A and B (much like with Spaniards or Latin Americans - where we all get conflated into a &quot;homogenous&quot; mental image - even though we can totally tell each other apart by other queues).<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> I mean, I thought she's a cool, empowered female character who overcomes horrible circumstances. Her skin color is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> But maybe I'm just reading too much into historical parallels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T20:23:16-07:00","id":1219165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1218658#post1218658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. A Song of Fire and Ice isn't anywhere near as clever as people like to pretend it is. A lot of the grittiness in the world only serves to paint our heroes with one colour and our villains with another.<br /> <br /> -The bedding ceremony exists in the form that it does so Ned Stark and Tyrion Lannister get to be gentlemen by refusing.<br /> -Primae Noctis was a thing in Westeros so Roose Bolton could highlight how evil he is.<br /> -Joffery Lannister needed to be an evil little shit to absolve Ned of the fact he basically put Cersei' children on Stannis' hit list.<br /> -Rape and accepting it is basically a shorthand for &amp;quot;this person is evil&amp;quot; its not a major part of Greyjoy and Dothraki culture dehumanising their enemies because apparently Daenerys can just tell them to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with a lot of this but I need to point out you\u2019re conflating the show without ASoIaF on a few points. Ned didn\u2019t forbid the bedding at his own wedding in ASoIaF, and Tyrion\u2019s treatment of Sansa is only gentlemanly in comparison to what was expected of him - stripping naked in bed with a... what was she then, 13 year old? fully aroused and saying you won\u2019t take her till she wants to would still be sexual abuse in a modern (and plenty of historic) social context.<br /> <br /> Tyrion being continuously presented as a modern moral man (except when the plot suddenly demands otherwise, as with Shay\u2019s death) is one of the show\u2019s obsessions that differs most strongly from the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-16-2018, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T01:48:15-07:00","id":1219206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219070#post1219070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no, Westeros does not need to lampshade every European interaction. It's a fantasy setting. Multi-year winters are more inspired by Fimbulwinter than by X, Y, Z, historical event. We should be thinking &quot;grim dark Nordic people seeing death and desperation&quot; not &quot;this show is making commentary on the Great Frost of 1709&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look back you'll see my issue was with people defending the world-building of Game of Thrones with &quot;it's historical&quot;. You're welcome to take the approach of &quot;it's fantasy, I haven't got to explain shit!&quot; but that's an entirely different discussion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T04:07:17-07:00","id":1219224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219070#post1219070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/I]<br /> (Tangent: And Dorne is Moorish Spain with a splash of Welsh/Cornish. Crazy how exotic one real-world peninsula can be.)<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Delurked just to ask, what Cornish or Welsh influence do you see in Dorne?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5001-soul_porpoise","name":"soul_porpoise","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T05:52:28-07:00","id":1219246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219165#post1219165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with a lot of this but I need to point out you\u2019re conflating the show without ASoIaF on a few points. Ned didn\u2019t forbid the bedding at his own wedding in ASoIaF, and Tyrion\u2019s treatment of Sansa is only gentlemanly in comparison to what was expected of him - stripping naked in bed with a... what was she then, 13 year old? fully aroused and saying you won\u2019t take her till she wants to would still be sexual abuse in a modern (and plenty of historic) social context.<br /> <br /> Tyrion being continuously presented as a modern moral man (except when the plot suddenly demands otherwise, as with Shay\u2019s death) is one of the show\u2019s obsessions that differs most strongly from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're right... a while ago I got some friend of mine to read the Black Company series and it's made me realise how good I've gotten at supressing extremely creepy moments in fantasy novels. This seems to be more of the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Storm of Swords</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roslin had gone white. Catelyn wondered whether it was the prospect of losing her maidenhead that frightened the girl, or the bedding itself. With so many siblings, she was not like to be a stranger to the custom, but it was different when you were the one being bedded. On Catelyn's own wedding night, Jory Cassell had torn her gown in his haste to get her out of it, and drunken Desmond Grell kept apologizing for every bawdy joke, only to make another. When Lord Destin had beheld her naked, he'd told Ned that her breasts were enough to make him wish he'd never been weaned.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T11:48:52-07:00","id":1219329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul_porpoise</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219224#post1219224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Delurked just to ask, what Cornish or Welsh influence do you see in Dorne?</div> </div> </div> </div>Colour me curious as well, as it's not as if the two are identical, any more than Irish and Scots are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T12:40:21-07:00","id":1219353,"title":"","content":"I've seen the Welsh/Dorne comparison made before <a href=\"https://inews.co.uk/culture/television/game-of-thrones-dorne-is-just-like-wales/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T12:41:02-07:00","id":1219354,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... well, I see their point about the Prince, but it's hardly unique. Most medieval Kingdoms had sub-Realms like this (because kingdoms were very politically messy).<br /> It certainly in no way gives me a Welsh feel. Not nearly enough rain. Or sheep.<br /> And certainly not Cornish.<br /> <br /> Tbh, Daenerys is based partly on Henry Tudor, who marched in to take over from the Lannisters and Starks... sorry, Lancasters and Yorks. His men marched under a dragon banner.<br /> So surely that makes the Targaeryans, with their dragon obsession, the Welsh! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (I'll remind anyone who doesn't know of it that this is the Welsh flag: <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Flag_of_Wales_2.svg/1200px-Flag_of_Wales_2.svg.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikiped...ales_2.svg.png</a> )<br /> <br /> (On a serious note: Martin tends to get bits of British history he likes or is interested in, mash it all together and change it around, add a splash of other history, mash it and mix it, throw in a bunch of his own ideas, and that's what you end up with. So you can find the odd bit and piece from different places, but I don't think you can really say that because he got the idea of Dorne having a Prince even though there's a King, from Welsh history, that makes Dorne based on Wales. It's not really enough. To get back to Lioness's point about people taking it like real history, I wouldn't want people looking at Dorne and thinking that's like Welsh history, because it's not. At all.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, on A Song of Ice and Fire more generally... it is better than the show in a lot of ways as have been mentioned, including the inclusion of non-white characters (partly because a number of characters are rather more white-skinned than I expected from the books). As Roswynn noted, there's a fair few non-white characters in the book that are played by white actors in the show. It's not brilliant, but better.<br /> Martin tends to vary a bit between deconstructing things and presenting them to entertain young male readers, so it's quite variable in how sensitive and realistic it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-16-2018, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:15:44-07:00","id":1219373,"title":"","content":"Watching GoT I've always gotten the impression that most of its cultures and societies are basically caricatures of real ones. Compelling and usually fairly nuanced caricatures, but caricatures nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:19:35-07:00","id":1219374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219354#post1219354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm... well, I see their point about the Prince, but it's hardly unique. Most medieval Kingdoms had sub-Realms like this (because kingdoms were very politically messy).<br /> It certainly in no way gives me a Welsh feel.<br /> And certainly not Cornish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, at best you've got a similarity in terms of the political structure, but as you say, that's not even particularly unusual (also lines of fealty in Wales were so messy that for a while you could argue that Anglesey was part of the Norwegian empire, though King Magnus didn't really enforce it). There's not even the slightist bit of Dorne that strikes me as culturally Welsh, in part because it's too bloody warm and not nearly rough enough. <br /> <br /> (It's also worth noting that 'Prince' in the case of the senior members of Welsh royal houses generally just meant leader [0], and that the 'Principality of Wales' never covered the entire territory of Wales [1], whereas the short-lived <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gruffydd_ap_Llywelyn#King_of_Wales_1055%E2%80%931063\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdom of Wales </a>actually did.)<br /> <br /> [0] Arguably 'a leader who doesn't want to provoke the perfidious Saeson by claiming to be King of the Britons, because they might think he was about to liberate Shropshire from the Norman/Saxon yoke'.<br /> <br /> [1] Under English rule the Principality was an area roughly corresponding to the present Fro Gymraeg that was under direct colonial rule by the English Crown; that changed under Henry VIII when the Laws of England and Wales Act unified the legal systems and abolished it. It's had no legal existence since, except apparently in the mind of Dafydd Ellis Thomas, and he's probably trolling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:20:47-07:00","id":1219375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watching GoT I've always gotten the impression that most of its cultures and societies are basically caricatures of real ones. Compelling and usually fairly nuanced caricatures, but caricatures nonetheless.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really surprising: as Salagism pointed out, why would you watch/read it for historical accuracy? It's a fantasy setting after all.<br /> <br /> But then, as Lioness said, some people will go &quot;ooh, it's so accurate!&quot; and think it shows things accurately.<br /> <br /> TBH, there's plenty of actual historical (rather than fantasy) shows that are just as bad in many ways. The middle ages is routinely depicted in an incredibly inaccurate way (and one that's harmful to modern society, because it reinforces certain stereotypes).<br /> If even historical fiction shows do a bad job, it's not really surprising that GoT doesn't do well either. In fact, it's sometimes better than some historical fiction I've seen; it does actually have some non-white people, cultural variation inside kingdoms, people not culturally identifying with the overall state as much as their local historical lands, it's not full of anachronistic racism, etc.<br /> <br /> Still. Would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-16-2018, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:26:31-07:00","id":1219381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219374#post1219374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [0] Arguably 'a leader who doesn't want to provoke the perfidious Saeson by claiming to be King of the Britons, because they might think he was about to liberate Shropshire from the Norman/Saxon yoke'.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Territorial claims is generally the main reason for declaring/not declaring yourself king, after all.<br /> <br /> Though the Scots sometimes got away with saying &quot;I'm King of the Scots but I admit the English King is totally awesome and better than me, and he's Top King of Britain.&quot;<br /> Still, King of the Scots doesn't really have the same territorial threat as claiming to be King of the Britons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:34:46-07:00","id":1219387,"title":"","content":"Obviously the OP doesn't seem to care, but I just wanted to say this has become the weirdest Conan thread ever for the past page and a half.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:36:41-07:00","id":1219389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219381#post1219381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Territorial claims is generally the main reason for declaring/not declaring yourself king, after all.<br /> <br /> Though the Scots sometimes got away with saying &quot;I'm King of the Scots but I admit the English King is totally awesome and better than me, and he's Top King of Britain.&quot;<br /> Still, King of the Scots doesn't really have the same territorial threat as claiming to be King of the Britons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Welsh also got away with being Kings of various Kingdoms until shortly after the Normans turned up, after which it got a bit fraught. I think the Tudors got a bit of milage out of being Kings/Queens of the Britons (at least in Welsh-facing propaganda) via references to King Arthur but my general opinion of them is unspeakably rude, so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:41:35-07:00","id":1219393,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I swear my posts break forums. I thought my post (above) hadn't gone through - so rewrote and trimmed it, waiting to give it a final glance this morning - and now I see the original is live. Ugh - I could have slept more! lol</div> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219206#post1219206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look back you'll see my issue was with people defending the world-building of Game of Thrones with &quot;it's historical&quot;. You're welcome to take the approach of &quot;it's fantasy, I haven't got to explain shit!&quot; but that's an entirely different discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an implied dichotomy that is unhelpful - and thus I want to avoid.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I feel that if we say:<br /> <br /> &quot;Game of Thrones is fiction!&quot;<ul><li>People will argue that &quot;so it's easy to write in more minorities!&quot;<ul><li><b>But that is not the point</b>. <i>No one </i>has the right to tell an artist what they must perform or write or produce - it's <i>their</i> reputation, <i>their</i> work, <i>their</i> legacy on the line. You can't force creatives to have ideas - nor should we expect people to produce work they're not inspired to produce.</li> </ul></li> </ul>&quot;Game of Thrones is based on history!&quot;<ul><li>People will argue that &quot;so every outlier example must be represented!&quot;<ul><li><b>But that is not the point</b>. He uses real-world tropes because they're intuitive to him and his audiences.<ul><li>And if he <b>does</b> use a trope - it's dishonest to suggest we need the Disney-approved version of those tropes - especially when the story isn't geographically nearby. As a Hispanic, I'm <b>impressed</b> with Dorne without needing to quibble over specifics.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b>Overall</b>, PoC are not &quot;noble savages&quot; who need glorified depictions that hide tropes our ancestors <i>sought</i>. The Mongols, Vikings and Nizari (Assassins) <b>alike</b> embraced their reputations - because it meant glory and fear and victims submitting with less effort. Italians to Romans, Mexicans to Aztecs, French to Napoleon, Turks to Ottomans &amp; Hittites - <b>all of these</b> cultures can reminisce on the &quot;glory days&quot; of their ancestors (no matter how bloody <b>all</b> of them were).<br /> <br /> A fantasy-setting featuring a continent-sized version of the British Isles doesn't <b>need</b> to go beyond that region. George R.R. Martin has <i>already</i> impressed me with his inclusion of &quot;us foreigners&quot; above and beyond what might be reciprocal.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">If I'm going to be offended? I'll start with Warhammer Fantasy.<br /> <br /> </span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Human?<br /> You must be a psuedo-English or psuedo-French member of a glorious empire.<br /> <br /> Edgy badass human?<br /> Chaos Warriors are Nords/Goths/Slavs.<br /> <br /> The implication being both &quot;the English come from the Saxons&quot; and &quot;Humans become Chaos Warriors&quot; - so both &quot;races&quot; amount to &quot;Northern Europeans are human&quot; and &quot;if we decide to go monstrous, we're more badass and feared than any other race&quot;.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><i>Everything goes downhill from there</i>.</b><br /> <br /> Southern Europeans (Portuguese, Spanish, Italian) are merged and caricatured into the Tileans - their architecture being &quot;the ruins of elves&quot;. So the real-life source of the Roman Empire.... is belittled into a bunch of incompetent humans squatting in the ruins of another race, a barely respectable &quot;buffer&quot; zone against Orcs and co....<br /> \u200b</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">...which is uncomfortable close to paralleling real-life racist Nords - who claim Southern Europeans have &quot;dirty blood&quot; (at best) or are an &quot;invasive species&quot; (at worst), squatting in the ruins of dead European civilizations. People who say Greeks, Italians and Spaniards are all really Turks, Libyans and Moors who wiped out the indigenous populations. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">This unflattering portrayal of their &quot;Southern European&quot; neighbors is just the start. Dwarves are &quot;gold-hungry clannish psuedo-Jews&quot; whose ghettos &quot;insidiously lurk beneath human kindgoms&quot;. Orcs are psuedo-African barbarians (because you can't even be bothered to differentiate between a <i>continent</i>). Non-Imperial native americans are deleted - with the &quot;big 3&quot; (Aztecs, Incas, Mayans) being merged into a race of Lizardfolk.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I mean </span></span><i>Jesus. </i><b>This </b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I can sink my teeth into criticizing. It doesn't merely show </span></span><i>disinterest</i><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> in foreign cultures (which is fine) - it </span></span><i>reduces</i><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> them to sub-human predatory monsters - </span></span><i>including</i><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> people who would be considered similar. </span></span><b>And that last part</b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> is the tell-tale sign. I would </span></span><b>expect</b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> an East-Asian to be baffled by a West-African - or for a Northern-European to be clueless about Aboriginals. </span></span><i>That's fine</i><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">. But when you turn your <i>neighbors</i> into monsters and sub-humans, <b>that</b> is when you go &quot;no wait a second - you <i>know</i> these people&quot;.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Game of Thrones is </span></span><i>far removed</i><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> from that level of criticism.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul_porpoise</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219224#post1219224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Delurked just to ask, what Cornish or Welsh influence do you see in Dorne?</div> </div> </div> </div>Language, to start. <br /> <br /> Wrong letters - Spanish has &quot;K&quot; and &quot;W&quot; for <i>loanwords </i>- so no &quot;Lewyn&quot;, no &quot;Yronwood&quot;, no &quot;Blackmont&quot;. And for Arabic, I don't see glottal stops (I still struggle to properly pronounce <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamza\" target=\"_blank\">Hamza</a>). Both serve as a kind of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shibboleth\" target=\"_blank\">Shibboleth</a>. Plus Quentyn, Lewyn, Arianne are pretty Welsh. And check out Doran's son <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tristan_and_Iseult\" target=\"_blank\">Trystane</a> -- and Oberyn as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oberon\" target=\"_blank\">Oberon</a>. <br /> <br /> Wrong rhythm as well. Spanish is more sing-songy. Names like <b>Mellario</b> and <b>Olyvar</b> sound good - &quot;Blackmont&quot; has <i>so many consonants</i>. If it means &quot;black mountain&quot;, the name would be &quot;monta\u00f1a negra&quot; (the &quot;\u00f1&quot; sounds like &quot;ne-ya&quot;). If my parents read <b>Trystane </b>or <b>Blackmont</b> &quot;as is&quot;, it'd probably sound like &quot;Tres-ta-neh&quot; (no silent vowels) or &quot;Bi-lac-mon&quot;. God forbid you have them try to pronounce <i>Twelfth</i> (&quot;wel-fff&quot;) or <i>Strength</i> (&quot;ste-ren&quot;). Get where I'm going with the consonant issue?<br /> <br /> Moreover the naming format - Spanish and Arabic are both <b>big</b> on lineage. Even if it has become muddled over time (especially in the New World) - I could still guestimate the &quot;home region&quot; of my friends. No shit a &quot;Couto&quot; is Galician-Portuguese (it's a small area near the border) or that a &quot;Useche&quot; is Basque. <br /> <br /> Also, history.<br /> <br /> Someone once compared the Targaryen / the Normans - trying to conquer the Dornes / the Welsh - both of which failed and then took centuries to turn around. The difference is that the Welsh kept fighting but the Dorne were absorbed by intermarriage. <b>Plus</b> the Welsh and Dorne refer to their rulers as &quot;princes&quot; - not Caliphs, Emirs, Sultans, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm not an expert on the Welsh!</b> So there are probably more parallels than I know about. But I can see a &quot;3rd influence&quot; that is neither Islamic nor Iberian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:47:56-07:00","id":1219396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219387#post1219387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously the OP doesn't seem to care, but I just wanted to say this has become the weirdest Conan thread ever for the past page and a half.</div> </div> </div> </div>I care. <br /> <br /> \u200bI'd also like to add that I wrote the original post after reading Phoenix on the Sword, the Scarlett Citadel, and the Tower of he Elephant, the misogyny got a lot more blatant after those three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:05:12-07:00","id":1219409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm going to be offended? I'll start with Warhammer Fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br /> Actually, you've made one mistake: the Spanish-expy is Estalia.<br /> Which is... barely detailed. Much less than Tilea (which is basically only Italian). Estalia is probably the least detailed, least important, least significant of Warhammer's human kingdoms.<br /> <br /> I will also point out that the Empire isn't pseudo-English, it's based on the Holy Roman Empire (ie Germans).<br /> <br /> The English-expy is Albion, a backward land of perpetual rain and fog populated by giants, cyclops, savage humans and Trueseers (druids, essentially).<br /> <br /> But your overall point is correct: the French and Germans get proper armies. The Eastern Europeans get smushed together and get 2 units and a special character. The Italians get an army in a magazine, not even a book.<br /> The Scandinavians get to be totally badass but also evil.<br /> Middle-Easterners are mentioned in the fluff, but are pretty insignificant; the main Middle-Eastern cultures are egyptian undead and evil babylonian slaver dwarves. There are virtually no South American or African humans (there are South American human... women. They have a Blood Bowl team. That's it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagism</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Language, to start.<br /> Plus Quentyn, Lewyn, Arianne are pretty Welsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lewyn is (well, Llewyn), I'll admit, as is Yronwood. Quentin is extremely English. Like, when I think of Quentin, I think of an upper-class English toff who went to Public School and is the son of a Baron, certainly not a Welshman. Welshmen have names like Dave, Rhodri, Dai, Matthew, David, James, Big Dai, Llewyn, Little Dai, Iozz, Dave, Dylan, Davidson, etc.<br /> (On a serious note, Quentin is actually not English but French. It comes from the Latin Quentinus. But I think of it as super upper class English. Like Archibald, or Benedict, or Bertie, or Cecil.)<br /> Arianne... I literally have no idea where that's from. Never heard it in real life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>I'm not an expert on the Welsh!</b> So there are probably more parallels than I know about. But I can see a &quot;3rd influence&quot; that is neither Islamic nor Iberian. </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, you've convinced me that George RR Martin might have thrown in 1 or 2 Welsh bits and bobs. But it's really minor. Honestly, I never noticed Lewyn or Yronwood, because Dorne is just so fundamentally... un-Welsh.<br /> <br /> Like... how could a land inspired by Wales ever, ever be hot and sunny with a desert? That's the complete opposite of Wales. It'd be like if you had an Arabic culture in the Canadian forest, or an Inuit-derived culture in the middle of Saudi Arabia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-16-2018, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:08:03-07:00","id":1219415,"title":"","content":"Quentyn and Oberyn/Oberon are not notably Welsh; Tristan is Welsh, granted; Lewyn and Arianne are only Welsh in the bad pseudo-Celtic fantasy sense [1]. Names show no sign of a voiceless alveolar fricative (the notorious 'll' which is a particular feature of Welsh) or similar consonantal complications; something like 'Blackmont' would be 'Mynydd Du' (in modern spelling; medieval orthography would be different) though there could be a translation convention for epithets, granted; there are no surnames, only epithets or patronymics, the latter of which you must be able to recite several generations back in order to establish a claim on land or as part of a family. (Eg. Gruffydd ap Owain [2] is from House Aberffraw, but you'd not call him Gruffydd Aberffraw unless it's his nickname and it certainly wouldn't substitute for a recitation of lineage in a legal context.)<br /> <br /> In addition, Dorne diverges greatly from Wales in terms of inheritance law -- it has gender neutral primogeniture. Wales had a gavelkind system -- and medieval Welsh politics makes no sense through the lens of primogeniture. Dorne seems to have no obsession with bards, and not nearly enough messy internicine warfare resulting from the inheritance system, so I'm not really seeing the alleged similarities beyond a sketchy 'well, this has a political set up that's kind of like Wales under Llywelyn the Great, but really nothing else is the same at all'.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Some example Welsh names can be found <a href=\"https://parallel.cymru/?p=6751\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, though some of them are a bit archaic, some of the given meanings/origins are suspect and the spelling isn't always reliable.<br /> <br /> [1] There are Welsh names similar to Arianne, but they're usually more like Arianrhod, Arianwen or something similar. 'Arianne' also conflicts with Welsh orthography; my non-expert guess is that it's more Latin in origin.<br /> <br /> [2] 'Gruffydd son of Owain'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":978,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","user":"Iozz-Sothoth","date":". 05-16-2018, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:09:12-07:00","id":1219417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219396#post1219396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I care.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd also like to add that I wrote the original post after reading Phoenix on the Sword, the Scarlett Citadel, and the Tower of he Elephant, the misogyny got a lot more blatant after those three.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked my friends what game to run next, and one suggested I run Conan. So I had a look at the Conan RPG... and man, it's racist. Not the most racist RPG I've read (it's not Myfarog), but any RPG that takes real-world race expies and gives some -2 Int or +2 Int is problematic.<br /> <br /> Not sure that's necessarily the original's fault (it's a long time since I read Conan), but it certainly doesn't have the excuse of being &quot;a product of its time&quot; as it was made in the 90s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:11:13-07:00","id":1219422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219415#post1219415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In addition, Dorne diverges greatly from Wales in terms of inheritance law -- it has gender neutral primogeniture. Wales had a gavelkind system (and medieval Welsh politics makes no sense through the lens of primogeniture.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, I'm not sure I can think of any fantasy books with medieval-esque settings written in the last few decades that have Gavelkind, even though it's a staple of fairytales and legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:29:43-07:00","id":1219437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219393#post1219393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[INDENT]I<br /> <br /> Language, to start. <br /> <br /> Wrong letters - Spanish has &amp;quot;K&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;W&amp;quot; for <i>loanwords </i>- so no &amp;quot;Lewyn&amp;quot;, no &amp;quot;Yronwood&amp;quot;, no &amp;quot;Blackmont&amp;quot;. And for Arabic, I don't see glottal stops (I still struggle to properly pronounce <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamza&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Hamza</a>). Both serve as a kind of <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shibboleth&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Shibboleth</a>. Plus Quentyn, Lewyn, Arianne are pretty Welsh. And check out Doran's son <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tristan_and_Iseult&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Trystane</a> -- and Oberyn as <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oberon&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Oberon</a>. <br /> <br /> Wrong rhythm as well. Spanish is more sing-songy. Names like <b>Mellario</b> and <b>Olyvar</b> sound good - &amp;quot;Blackmont&amp;quot; has <i>so many consonants</i>. If it means &amp;quot;black mountain&amp;quot;, the name would be &amp;quot;monta\u00f1a negra&amp;quot; (the &amp;quot;\u00f1&amp;quot; sounds like &amp;quot;ne-ya&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. If my parents read <b>Trystane </b>or <b>Blackmont</b> &amp;quot;as is&amp;quot;, it'd probably sound like &amp;quot;Tres-ta-neh&amp;quot; (no silent vowels) or &amp;quot;Bi-lac-mon&amp;quot;. God forbid you have them try to pronounce <i>Twelfth</i> (&amp;quot;wel-fff&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> or <i>Strength</i> (&amp;quot;ste-ren&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Get where I'm going with the consonant issue?<br /> <br /> Moreover the naming format - Spanish and Arabic are both <b>big</b> on lineage. Even if it has become muddled over time (especially in the New World) - I could still guestimate the &amp;quot;home region&amp;quot; of my friends. No shit a &amp;quot;Couto&amp;quot; is Galician-Portuguese (it's a small area near the border) or that a &amp;quot;Useche&amp;quot; is Basque. <br /> <br /> Also, history.<br /> <br /> Someone once compared the Targaryen / the Normans - trying to conquer the Dornes / the Welsh - both of which failed and then took centuries to turn around. The difference is that the Welsh kept fighting but the Dorne were absorbed by intermarriage. <b>Plus</b> the Welsh and Dorne refer to their rulers as &amp;quot;princes&amp;quot; - not Caliphs, Emirs, Sultans, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm not an expert on the Welsh!</b> So there are probably more parallels than I know about. But I can see a &amp;quot;3rd influence&amp;quot; that is neither Islamic nor Iberian.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what has any of that to do with Cornwall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5001-soul_porpoise","name":"soul_porpoise","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T17:03:43-07:00","id":1219479,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219409#post1219409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are South American human... women. They have a Blood Bowl team. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love being simultaneously infuriated, disappointed, cheaply titillated and <i>laughing out loud</i>. Oh my god. Thank you for the corrections (and additional notes) - I'm fairly sure I blocked most of it out, with Warhammer just being 3edgy5me<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219409#post1219409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like... how could a land inspired by Wales ever, ever be hot and sunny with a desert? That's the complete opposite of Wales. It'd be like if you had an Arabic culture in the Canadian forest, or an Inuit-derived culture in the middle of Saudi Arabia.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do the Welsh relate-and-differ-to the Irish? Because.... <a href=\"https://www.irishtimes.com/news/genetic-studies-show-our-closest-relatives-are-found-in-galicia-and-the-basque-region-1.700877\" target=\"_blank\">check this out</a>. Maybe?<br /> <br /> Dorne isn't just desert - the Red Mountains divide the region from the continent. And despite the &quot;red stone&quot;, it is variously described as &quot;forested&quot;, &quot;fertile&quot;, &quot;meadows&quot;, &quot;sweet and green grass&quot;, &quot;hidden valleys&quot; - there are people who live there. Well people think Iberia is Arid / Mediterranean / Continental..... but in the north it is mountainous, oceanic, forested, cold. <br /> <br /> And while Dorne seems to just have the mega-sized &quot;Red Mountains&quot; - Iberia has four major mountain-regions hip-to-hip in the North. <br /> <br /> The Pyrenees in the NE divide Spain from the rest of Europe (much like the Red Mountains do overall). The Canabrian Mountains (in the center) were allegedly &quot;so high and unreachable&quot; during the Caliphate, the Christian Kingdoms there rallied forces (so the Spanish version of Skyreach?). And then you have the Galician Massif (NW) and Basque Mountains (C/NE) with the heavy Celtic DNA (at least 2,000+ years, and they're more closely related to the Irish than they are to other Spaniards? <b>that</b> is a testament to clannishness).<br /> <br /> It's not Welsh nor Irish nor Scottish.<br /> <br /> But if George R.R. Martin can't differentiate La Coru\u00f1a from Navarra - <b>but</b> knows there's some kind of Celtic mixed in - then I think it's &quot;close enough&quot; to sprinkle in whatever he does know that approximates it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219415#post1219415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(everything)</div> </div> </div> </div><b>You rock</b>. <br /> <br /> Sometimes I worry I'm geeking out too much over (regional niches here) and then people like you post awesome (regional niches there).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul_porpoise</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219437#post1219437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what has any of that to do with Cornwall?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beats me! I just know it's not Spanish/Arabic. But as others have linked - and <a href=\"https://www.quora.com/Is-Dorne-based-on-Cornwall-in-A-Song-of-Fire-and-Ice\" target=\"_blank\">here's another</a> - a lot of people seem to see Welsh and Cornish (Dornish) politics painted over a psuedo-Iberian landscape.<br /> <br /> Maybe we'll get lucky and see more regional posts there.<br /> <br /> My brain is Latin America and Iberia (comfortably) - large swaths of the Islamic world (mutual history &amp; studying Arabic) - and tiny pinches of West Africa (Caribbean cultural influence). <b>Cornwall</b> and <b>Latvia</b> are as exotic to me as <b>Azerbaijan</b> or <b>Djibouti</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219396#post1219396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I care.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd also like to add that I wrote the original post after reading Phoenix on the Sword, the Scarlett Citadel, and the Tower of he Elephant, the misogyny got a lot more blatant after those three.</div> </div> </div> </div>How bad is it? Are we talking <i>characters and setting</i> or <i>author</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T18:59:21-07:00","id":1219508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219479#post1219479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How bad is it? Are we talking <i>characters and setting</i> or <i>author</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Looking back over the other stories I read:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">In<i> The Black Colossus</i> the gorgeous redheaded princess hires Conan to fight a war for her and at the end Conan rescues her from her captors and she responds with something like \u201cStay here in this prison for a bit and let me be yours. When we leave I\u2019ll have to be a ruler again\u201d. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">In the <i>Slithering Shadow</i> Conan is dragging a pretty girl with him through the desert despite her uselessness for non-sexy pursuits. He finds ancient city full of dreaming people, the most dominant woman of the city tries to kill Conan\u2019s girl so he\u2019ll stay with her because she\u2019s so turned on by his virility. Conan and his girl leave. Conan mocks the girl about her vanity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">In <i>The Pool of the Black One</i> Sancha the delectably sexy woman and paramour of the pirate captain is lounging with all of her skin showing on the deck of the pirate ship when Conan swims aboard. Within a few days she\u2019s giddy with the thought of Conan killing her man so that she could be his. Then it happens, also ancient evil creatures.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I don't recall anything drastically sexist from <i>Rouges in the House</i>.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">In <i>Gods of the North</i> a vision of feminine physical beauty comes to Conan as he lies wounded on a battlefield. The vision is a supernatural creature come who has come to torment Conan with her sexiness. Conan has doesn't take that sort of crap, and he chases her down in a lust crazed rage killing her frost giant brothers, and starting to rape her until her divine father spirits her away. (It starts as the myth of the selkie or the nymph but it gets turned around because Conan is so manly.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Shadows in the Moonlight</i> Conan rescues a scantily clad woman from his enemy, she considers Conan\u2019s company marginally better than being recaptured. Then they go to an island full of ancient evil. With Conan\u2019s example she becomes moderately less incompetent. They live, she gives herself to him.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Queen of the Black Coast</i> A scantily clad white woman commands a crew of black skinned pirates, they take over the ship on which Conan is sailing. The white girl commands her pirates to keep Conan alive so she can have him. Conan and the woman pirate about for a bit, then they head up river to an ancient pyramid filled with evil sorcery. Everyone but Conan dies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>The Devil in Iron:</i> Men realize that they can\u2019t beat Conan\u2019s troops with Conan in charge. They arrange a fake parley where they parade a beautiful blonde woman prisoner whom they force to make advances at Conan in front him while they fail to make a deal. Later the scheming men send a letter purportedly from the blonde saying \u201cI\u2019ve escaped to this deserted island please come for me you big hunk of man\u201d Conan heads for the island, the schemers hope to catch him there while he\u2019s alone and they have scores of archers. The blonde coincidentally escapes and\u2026 I\u2019m not kidding here...goes to the same deserted island. There\u2019s ancient evil sorcery on the island, Conan escapes, he saves the helpless girl and wins her affections, everyone else dies.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm most of the way through the next story, it doesn't look like a change in direction.<br /> <br /> \u200bSome of the women have some agency, they all however are in the stories primarily to serve as a sexy reward for our protagonist, none of them end the story having any goal more important to them than servicing Conan's penis.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think that most of the racial stuff flys by me as I'm not connecting the fantasy racial names to any real world people and &quot;brown skin&quot; to my mind can describe pretty much anyone from a tan swede to pretty darn black.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 05-16-2018, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T19:54:46-07:00","id":1219520,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it's not like he brought along the girl with him in <i>Slithering Shadow</i> for giggles; if he'd left her in the desert, she definitely would have died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T22:13:50-07:00","id":1219536,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar872_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"872\" data-vbnamecard=\"872\">Apromor</a> <br /> <br /> Honest question - is misogyny the right word? <br /> <br /> I mean, okay - stories about <i>Conan</i> have little interest in people not named <i>Conan</i> - but the film <i>Get Out</i> was also focused on the male lead (complete with the femme fatale who only exists to seduce and prey upon guys - and who has to be slain in the end). Does this mean <i>Get Out</i> was misogynistic? <br /> <hr /><br /> Let's tackle some of your examples:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Black Colossus:</b><br /> Dominant female ally reduces protagonist to fuckboy. Then goes back to being Queen.<br /> <br /> <b>Queen of the Black Coast:</b><br /> Dominant female villain reduces protagonist to fuckboy.<br /> <br /> <b>Pool of the Black One:</b><br /> Treacherous female pirate sees male as expendable - and protagonist as new fuckboy.<br /> <br /> <b>Gods of the North:</b><br /> Predatory female monster fails to victimize protagonist - but her 2 brothers die. <br /> <br /> <b>Shadows in the Moonlight &amp; Slithering Shadow:</b><br /> Characters who would have died off (if born male) - escape by virtue of sexuality. Protagonists looks down upon their weakness - but still affords them special protection a male would never receive - because men are generally expected to be stupid enough to think with their dicks.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Is this misogyny? <br /> <br /> If males <b>die</b> left-and-right ; the male protagonist is reduced to a sexy object ; and half the women are in positions of power over everyone else....wouldn't it be equally (if not more) misandryst? <br /> <br /> And what are some of the presuppositions in your review?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Villainous Females:</b></span><br /> Coast Queen (pirates), Black One (pirates) and Gods of the North (monsters) don't depict victims - it sounds like they depict predators. By your own description, it's the men around them that die first and most often. How is this misogynistic?<br /> <br /> Going to personal examples - <i>a couple people I know</i> (who I don't wingman with) - drink and drug <i>a lot</i>. And <b>not by coincidence</b>, the women they hang out with also favor booze and drugs. And they cheat on the girls because &quot;all women are liars&quot; - and the girls cheat on them because &quot;all men are liars&quot; - and then, if I'm unlucky enough to be around, I get to hear <b>both </b>genders drunkenly lament their shitty situation (wishing they could &quot;meet a nice person&quot; without the self-awareness to realize that <i>they themselves aren't nice people</i>).<br /> <br /> Is it misogynistic to depict <i><b>female <u>pirates</u></b></i>as unethical and vice-driven? <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Empowered Females:</b></span><br /> Last year, a female friend of mine got divorced after almost a decade with an ingrate. She is better educated, better paid, better looking - and he cheated on her. In response she spent a year with a new fuckboy every 2 months - because <i>they were hot</i> and <i>she was in control</i> and <i>women like sex too</i>. She said it was an ego boost and reassertion of her wants (because she had once favored athletes - then dated this out-of-shape ingrate - and she wanted to prove to herself that she could still have a hunk grovel for her).<br /> <br /> Was my female friend being &quot;misogynistic&quot; for giving a few hunks easy sex and then ditching them? <br /> <br /> Are women in power not allowed to enjoy the occasional fuckboy?<br /> <br /> Is there something <i>woman hating</i> about female characters reducing Conan's worth to his penis?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Selection Bias &amp; Victims:</b></span><br /> If my friends - or Conan - randomly pulled women off a crowd to &quot;rescue them&quot; from their &quot;own incompetence&quot;? Sure - that's trash.<br /> <br /> But one of my friends is a firefighter - so <i>by virtue of selection bias</i>, <b>anyone</b> he is called to rescue is someone <i>incompetent </i>enough to need outside help. Likewise, anyone who needs a doctor to save them from an illness is <i>incompetent</i> enough to need outside aid. It's not an insult to be incompetent at something. So why shouldn't Conan see as incompetent people who required his rescue in the first place?<ul><li>And by extension, the firefighter friend was a chubby geek growing up - only in college did he get fit and find his calling. So not only is he the muscular, uniformed guy girls see when adrenaline is pumping and they need help - but now <i>they ask for his number</i> or even <i>Snapchat offering to blow him</i>. He gets pink-faced, unsure how to respond half the time. Is he misogynistic for attracting female aggression?</li> </ul>A less flattering example is my cousin, also hot (lifelong gym rat) - who isn't too bright - but in turn, surrounds himself with women who aren't too bright. It's not misogynistic to say the whole crowd is fairly stupid - it's <i>selection bias</i> that stupid people congregate to do stupid things with each other. Smart women certainly exist - they just don't fall for his bullshit (unless they want to use him for a 1-night-shag). They don't exist in <i>his story</i> because they don't need him.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not trying to be coy - but I really, really, really want to be <b>precise </b>with words.<br /> <br /> Stories of mass male slaughter... with dominant females reducing the hero to a sex-toy.... or obtaining special protection <i>that he wouldn't give males</i>.... seems a lot more like misandry than misogyny. Men are expendable and easy to manipulate and willing to risk death if tempted properly.<br /> <br /> You make the stories sound dull and predictable and they probably are. But is this <i>hateful</i> toward women? Or is the hero of the story simply surrounded by vile people all around?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">For comparison, I point back to the Game of Thrones vs Warhammer talk.<br /> <br /> I would never consider George R.R. Martin's work <i>racist</i> or <i>exclusionary</i> - he quite clearly defined Westeros as a continent-sized version of the British Isles - <b>and yet</b> expanded representation to nudge in non-local cultures with very &quot;close to history&quot; real-world parallels. Game of Thrones being &quot;hyper focused locally&quot; could excuse offensive cultural inaccuracies about foreigners (and yet he doesn't play on them).<br /> <br /> I <i>would</i> take issue with Warhammer - not merely for glorifying Germans as the &quot;one true human empire&quot; - but for turning non-German European-neighbors as insignificant footnotes living in squalor - and for expanding the map further just to turn non-Europeans into monsters. The <b>reverse</b> of Game of Thrones, the focus is <i>global</i> - so you <i>expect</i> an interest in other peoples - and yet Warhammer only reduces non-Germans to either &quot;incompetents&quot; or &quot;cannon-fodder monsters&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm not doubting that you might see misogyny in Conan - but <b>are you sure these examples <i>hate women</i>?</b> I'm looking for Warhammer-tier &quot;all women are idiots&quot; or &quot;all women are weak&quot; or &quot;all women are vile&quot;.... not Game of Thrones tier &quot;we have a little of everything&quot;.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Just a thought.<br /> <br /> <b>Obligatory Disclaimer:</b> I read/write English a lot - but it's not my default - especially in areas of slurs/insults/etc. What's offensive in (culture A) might be a virtue in (culture B). So <b>if</b> there is something hateful - and I'm not grasping it - I'd love to see what you're seeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T22:24:16-07:00","id":1219538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219479#post1219479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bBeats me! I just know it's not Spanish/Arabic. But as others have linked - and <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.quora.com/Is-Dorne-based-on-Cornwall-in-A-Song-of-Fire-and-Ice&amp;quot;]here's</a> another[/URL] - a lot of people seem to see Welsh and Cornish (Dornish) politics painted over a psuedo-Iberian landscape.<br /> <br /> Maybe we'll get lucky and see more regional posts there.<br /> <br /> My brain is Latin America and Iberia (comfortably) - large swaths of the Islamic world (mutual history &amp; studying Arabic) - and tiny pinches of West Africa (Caribbean cultural influence). <b>Cornwall</b> and <b>Latvia</b> are as exotic to me as <b>Azerbaijan</b> or <b>Djibouti</b>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, did you read the replies to tat question on quota? The idea was pretty much dismissed out of hand for a good reason. <br /> <br /> You're conflating Wales and Cornwall when they are two different regions with honestly very little in common. Cornwall's culture and history share a fair bit with the Breton's and God help us, Devon, but the Welsh are just more emmetts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5001-soul_porpoise","name":"soul_porpoise","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T03:38:47-07:00","id":1219569,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> perhaps misogyny isn't the right word. In the stories the women, even the powerful ones, are presented as sex objects first and anything else is secondary. The stories aren't nice to the non-Conan men either.<br /> <br /> \u200b(also while they do seem to be repetitive,I wouldn't describe them as boring... wait I apparently just did exactly that - it was unintentional. \u200bThat was a list of summaries of how the stories could be seen as degrading to women not an attempt to describe them as a whole.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 02-09-2019, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T07:28:58-07:00","id":1219628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul_porpoise</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219538#post1219538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the Welsh are just more emmetts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually did make me laugh out loud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T07:48:40-07:00","id":1219637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219479#post1219479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI love being simultaneously infuriated, disappointed, cheaply titillated and <i>laughing out loud</i>. Oh my god. Thank you for the corrections (and additional notes) - I'm fairly sure I blocked most of it out, with Warhammer just being 3edgy5me</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably forgot to mention that North America is inhabited almost entirely by Dark Elves: evil pale-skinned people who love murder, torture, sacrificing people to their dark god, some more murder, and drugs.<br /> I guess they do have human slaves though. But such slaves are always depicted as being white-skinned too.<br /> <br /> As a 12 year old, when I started playing Warhammer, it wasn't quite so obvious to me, but over time it became more and more obvious.<br /> <br /> I suspect when originally thought of it wasn't supposed to be like that: really far-off places actually do include humans: there's an India-land, China-land and Japan-land. And there is an Arabia-land with genies and sorcerers on flying carpets, although it's been talked about less and less. Also, the first race that lived outside Europe-land, High Elves, lived in a magical kingdom right in the middle of the Atlantic (I guess to make it Atlantis-esque, or like Tolkien). So they weren't even taking the space of any real ethnic group.<br /> I think what happened is there were two human armies (Arthurian-French knights and the Holy Roman Empire) and so the company decided they needed non-human armies. They ended up then filling all the other parts of the world with strange monsters, rather than black people, Amerindians, etc, because it worked better commercially and they were more concerned with that than presenting a balanced picture of various ethnic groups.<br /> <br /> (I will note one other thing: the Dwarves in Warhammer aren't depicted as Jewish, they're depicted as Viking-esque.)<br /> <br /> Oddly, 40K has generally received far more criticism than Warhammer Fantasy. Somewhat fair (the most popular human army, Space Marines, had a &quot;No girls allowed&quot; rule introduced during the 2nd edition of the game for... no real reason really*), but its culture and ethnicities are a fair bit more mixed, even with all the German/Latin names. If you want to play a black human army, or an Asian human army, that's fine, you just paint your models that way. Or you could make them mixed.<br /> And the aliens have cultures that aren't based on human ethnic groups.<br /> Unlike Warhammer with its Egyptian and Romanian undead, South American lizardmen, Middle Eastern evil Dwarves, etc.<br /> <br /> *I ran a 40k rpg for a year. I introduced a female Space Marine as an NPC, from a 1st edition chapter. The players all shrugged and went &quot;yeah, seems fair,&quot; except one who was all &quot;what? Girls can't be Space Marines! It says so in the book!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagism</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If males <b>die</b> left-and-right ; the male protagonist is reduced to a sexy object ;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there you run into the issue that often when male protagonists are &quot;reduced to a sexy object&quot;... they're not really reduced to it. The books were written by a man, for male readers. It's more a power fantasy: the protagonist is so amazing and powerful and awesome that all the women want to fuck him. He's not being reduced or objectified, because he has a lot of agency.<br /> It can be a fine line of course between being super-sexy as a good thing, and being super-sexy as objectification. The question generally revolves around whether that's all they do, and how much choice do they have.<br /> Is the character purely sexy, or can he/she do other things?<br /> Does the character have agency in other matters? Or do they just follow the other characters providing sexiness?<br /> Are they really a character, or just a convenient sex receptacle for the protagonist?<br /> <br /> As to all the other men dying... I think this isn't misandry so much as an alpha male/beta male thing. Conan (who the reader is invited to imagine themselves as) is super awesome and brilliant, while other men are losers and die because they're not as good as Conan.<br /> (I'm exaggerating here for hyperbole.)<br /> They don't die because they're men, they die because they're neither Conan or a girl he wants to have sex with (though sometimes the girl dies too, because she's not Conan).<br /> (Of course, there's also an element here of just ending that story. People die so Conan can start the next story fresh, providing more creative freedom to the author, rather than having to keep the same characters following Conan.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-17-2018, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T14:05:42-07:00","id":1219782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul_porpoise</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219538#post1219538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, did you read the replies to that question on quota? The idea was pretty much dismissed out of hand for a good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slow your roll, my friend. I already admitted I'm a non-Brit - so I was hardly trying to make the <i>authoritative declaration</i> that it's Wales or Cornwall. If that's what you interpreted, I apologize.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the link - and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=dorne+cornwall&amp;oq=dorne+cornwall\" target=\"_blank\">others like it</a> - is to say &quot;the rumor mill points to Cornwall &amp; Wales&quot;. Lioness confirmed it was a prevalent conversation - The Wizard of Oz agreed and disagreed with parts - and Iozz-Sothot hit me in my sweet spot with linguistic insight and cultural differences (actually educating me, framing his rebuttal in a way that mirrored my objections to the purely Iberian parts). If you think it should be dismissed &quot;with good reason&quot; - please feel free to share your insight! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219637#post1219637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what happened is there were two human armies (Arthurian-French knights and the Holy Roman Empire) and so the company decided they needed non-human armies. They ended up then filling all the other parts of the world with strange monsters, rather than black people, Amerindians, etc, because it worked better commercially and they were more concerned with that than presenting a balanced picture of various ethnic groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair shake. One of my friends introduced us to HeroQuest - and while not <i>offensive</i>, some of the presuppositions &quot;back then&quot; seem primitive. Old games were still fumbling with ideas.<br /> <br /> I just cringe when things carry on to modernity. Bikini-armor is a pet peeve. And even modern D&amp;D has some cringey monster-origins (I think Banshees are Elven women who are cursed... because they weren't nice enough? did a deity literally doom women to eternal suffering because they <i>didn't smile enough</i>?). FML.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219637#post1219637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I will note one other thing: the Dwarves in Warhammer aren't depicted as Jewish, they're depicted as Viking-esque.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Maybe I'm conflating them with Tolkien? I know it wasn't my idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219637#post1219637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there you run into the issue that often when male protagonists are &quot;reduced to a sexy object&quot;... they're not really reduced to it. The books were written by a man, for male readers. It's more a power fantasy: the protagonist is so amazing and powerful and awesome that all the women want to fuck him. He's not being reduced or objectified, because he has a lot of agency. It can be a fine line of course between being super-sexy as a good thing, and being super-sexy as objectification. The question generally revolves around whether that's all they do, and how much choice do they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent points! But this brings me back to the &quot;real life analogies&quot; I thought of.<br /> <br /> My divorced-friend on her hunk frenzy? <b>All</b> those guys probably thought they had agency - but <b>all</b> of them were used. We don't need a dichotomy of victor/victim, winner/loser. In <i><b>their</b></i> life story, they were hot guys banging chicks - in <b>her</b> life story, they were footnotes she always intended to dispose of. Both sides can enjoy their own perspectives in private and be happy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219637#post1219637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the character purely sexy, or can he/she do other things? Does the character have agency in other matters? Or do they just follow the other characters providing sexiness?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>B\u00ealit </b>(the Pirate Queen) sailed from Kush to Zingara, respected by her crew. Conan (from a landlocked country) only proceeded to a career in piracy <b>after</b> learning from her. Is that not agency, authority, respect?<br /> <br /> <b>Yasmela </b>(the Princess, King's sister) didn't need rescue - it was her brother, Khossus, who had been kidnapped. Yasmela <i>hired</i> Conan <b>and</b> enjoyed his fuckboy talents - and when <i>Conan</i> suggested marriage, she clarified that she was <i>much too busy</i> with her own career (affairs of state). She says that if Khossus returned, she could consider it...... and then Khossus <i>refuses</i> to give the blessing for the marriage, and while agreeing that Conan merits wealth, also denigates him - because it'd be unseemingly for a mere commoner to become General. So Conan fucks off from there. <b>So Conan</b> banged a princess and thought he might become a General or Prince - <b>instead</b>, after risking his life, the relationship is rejected, the position isn't offered, and at best they'll let him become an advisor to some other noble who can claim credit. Is this a power fantasy? I wonder if Yasmela knew her brother wouldn't approve....<br /> <br /> <b>Sancha</b> (the Pirate's Paramour) isn't some traitorous, sex-crazed waif. She was the duke's daughter from Kordova (Cordoba?) - charming, intellectual and analytical. It was Zaporavo (the pirate) who kidnapped her and used her for sex - and when Conan kills Zaporavo - she latches on to him. Is this a fault? It sounds like an Eclipse surrounded by Night &amp; Dawn Castes (so to speak). I'm sure she had her own adventures when she returned to civilization where her skill-set matters.<br /> <br /> Have you read Neil Gaiman's <a href=\"http://www.neilgaiman.com/mediafiles/exclusive/shortstories/emerald.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">A Study in Emerald</a>?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Gaiman needed to pastiche Sherlock Holmes with the Cthulhu Mythos - but how do you combine &quot;unknowable horror&quot; with a detective who can &quot;solve anything via logic&quot;? One will trample the other. <br /> <br /> So he misleads the reader... until the end, when you realize it's Moriarty dealing with Lovecraftian horror - and Holmes <i>is among those horrors</i>, as a sort of &quot;cover story&quot; or &quot;alibi&quot; man, his rational mundane explanations concealing the otherworldly. In this pastiche, Cthulhu remains unknowable - and Holmes remains all-knowing (because he's secretly in on the secret).<br /> <br /> How is this relevant?<br /> <br /> <b>My point is</b> a story about Sherlock Holmes is about Sherlock - and a story about Conan is about Conan.<br /> <br /> But nothing forbade Neil Gaiman from grabbing a secondary character and <i>giving him his own story. </i>Moriarty doesn't need Holmes to glorify him - he just needs ink and paper devoted <i>to him</i>. Moriarty <i>has always been</i> a character of his own - and it's not a Sherlock story's responsibility to cater to Moriarty.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219637#post1219637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to all the other men dying... I think this isn't misandry so much as an alpha male/beta male thing. Conan (who the reader is invited to imagine themselves as) is super awesome and brilliant, while other men are losers and die because they're not as good as Conan. (I'm exaggerating here for hyperbole.) They don't die because they're men, they die because they're neither Conan or a girl he wants to have sex with (though sometimes the girl dies too, because she's not Conan).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you. And I'm not actually offended or concerned with misandry.<br /> <br /> I just find....dissonance?.... in worrying about one gender while the other gender as expendable. This doesn't scream &quot;Conan is about hating women&quot; so much as &quot;Conan is about Conan - fuck everyone else, regardless of gender&quot;. It's self-centered and vain at worst? But so are all the other characters who don't give a wit about Conan.<br /> <br /> I mean, I love having these kinds of discussions - but <b>both</b> genders need to be considered.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take the &quot;wage gap&quot; - another area people often scream &quot;misogyny.&quot;<br /> <br /> But let's start with the fact that countries that have <i>maximized</i> gender equality face the <b>paradox</b> of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p5LRdW8xw70\" target=\"_blank\"><b>more</b> gender differences</a> in career choice (men double-down on engineering, science construction - &quot;things&quot; ... while women double-down on &quot;people&quot;). It's the <b>least</b> equal countries where women pursue &quot;manly&quot; careers as a way of independicizing themselves from men.<br /> <br /> So why are there differences in career-choice? We need to look at <a href=\"http://www.apa.org/news/press/releases/2011/08/mental-illness.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">gender differences in mental illness</a> (men = antisocial, women = neuroticism); the theory that autism is just &quot;<a href=\"http://cogsci.bme.hu/~ivady/bscs/read/bc.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">more extreme maleness</a>&quot;; hormonal differences in interests (higher testosterone? <i>things</i> - lower testosterone? <i>people</i>). <br /> <br /> This doesn't mean there aren't women interested in engineering.<br /> <br /> But it's not a man's fault if they don't pursue those fields in equal numbers.<br /> <br /> Inevitably someone says it's about education - but over a decade ago, <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2006/07/09/education/09college.html\" target=\"_blank\">women were outperforming men</a> - and today there are colleges where only <a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/education/archive/2017/08/why-men-are-the-new-college-minority/536103/\" target=\"_blank\">16% of the campus is male</a>. When women do best in education, how is it a guy's fault if they decide to pursue something else?<br /> <br /> And then there's <a href=\"https://www.dol.gov/wb/stats/most_common_occupations_for_women.htm\" target=\"_blank\">occupations by Gender</a>. Notice a lot of female jobs are &quot;interested in people&quot; - teachers, nurses, administrative, sales. Notice a lot of male jobs are &quot;interested in things&quot; - labor, building, driving, factories, computers. It's not a lack-of-education preventing women from being truck drivers, construction laborers or factory workers.<br /> <br /> <b>Now</b> factory in that 93% of workplace fatalities are men - because there are tons of low-education, high-danger, high-paying jobs guys volunteer for. Go <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2004/07/21/us/it-s-a-long-lonely-search-for-men-looking-for-love-in-alaska.html\" target=\"_blank\">work in Alaska</a> to see the living-conditions men will accept but women won't. If you <i>need equality</i>, when do we start conscripting women into becoming coal miners ($70-90K), oil rig workers ($65-108K), landfill gas collectors ($72-108K), construction foremen ($56K+), <i>deer urine farmers</i> (ridiculous as it sounds)? Even low-paying jobs (like drivers) can make money on the side.<br /> <br /> <b>And yes</b>, inequality exists - compare Mexican <a href=\"http://serendip.brynmawr.edu/sci_cult/courses/knowbody/f04/web2/sjorgensen.html\" target=\"_blank\">Mauqiladoras</a> (which deliberately favor women and exclude men <b>because</b> they are less likely to protest or demand better conditions &amp; pay). Are the men (who can't even get hired) responsible for the women (who dominate the factories) not asking for raises? If gender discrimination was legal (which it isn't), we'd see more scenarios like Mexico.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> So the wage gap isn't merely comparing 2 numbers - because each gender is also prioritizing different things. True equality isn't &quot;women exclusively pursue high-prestige office jobs&quot; - it also means &quot;more women doing dirty, dangerous well-paying jobs&quot;. Or factor in differences in work preference and maternity leave (I think one issue in those <i>super equal</i> Nordic countries is women preferring part-time work so they can enjoy non-work-related things.... meanwhile men <i>become their jobs</i>).<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> <b>Bringing it all back to Conan</b>, <u>real misogyny</u> requires <i>hating women</i>. That's the definition. And it exists in the real-world.<br /> <br /> But if Conan treats men &amp; women equally shitty then <i>that's equality. <br /> <br /> And thus far</i>, the women seem to have an unfair advantage - I'm fairly sure <i>most people</i> would prefer to give a barbarian a beej over being left behind or murdered. I would master the art of beejing if it meant not being abandoned and left to die with everyone else. Beejes all day.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm sure there are more examples that will arise that seem problematic - I just don't want to be loose with definitions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T15:11:33-07:00","id":1219803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219782#post1219782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slow your roll, my friend. I already admitted I'm a non-Brit - so I was hardly trying to make the <i>authoritative declaration</i> that it's Wales or Cornwall. If that's what you interpreted, I apologize.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the link - and <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.com/search?q=dorne+cornwall&amp;oq=dorne+cornwall&amp;quot;]others</a> like it[/URL] - is to say &amp;quot;the rumor mill points to Cornwall &amp; Wales&amp;quot;. Lioness confirmed it was a prevalent conversation - The Wizard of Oz agreed and disagreed with parts - and Iozz-Sothot hit me in my sweet spot with linguistic insight and cultural differences (actually educating me, framing his rebuttal in a way that mirrored my objections to the purely Iberian parts). If you think it should be dismissed &amp;quot;with good</div> </div> </div> </div>Lioness confirmed the discussion about Wales was a thing, not Cornwall. <br /> <br /> You've presented two links, one a question without any backing evidence and one that mostly rides on the fact Dorne is a peninsula and Dornish rhymes with Cornish. They are both also bipeds, big whoop. <br /> <br /> The only substantial bits of an argument there (language, later intervention) apply just as much to Wales as Conrwall and since Martin admitted basing it partly on Wales, seems far more likely that is the source for this as well. <br /> <br /> As to shooting down the arguments, you made the extraordinary claim, you bring the alleged proof and I'll tell you if it's worth anything, but I'm not going to go through the entirely of Cornish culture and how it doesn't match Dorne. <br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, Baron-Cohen's male brain theory has failed to gain much in the way of traction, especially regarding testosterone levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5001-soul_porpoise","name":"soul_porpoise","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T17:08:51-07:00","id":1219830,"title":"","content":"This thread never ceases to amaze.<br /> <br /> I've thought about picking up the Modiphius Conan books to draw on them for inspiration for things and places in Exalted too, since the people working on it are apparently Conan enthusiasts, it could be a useful resource!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":23657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","user":"VioletDreamer","date":". 05-17-2018, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T05:30:51-07:00","id":1219931,"title":"","content":"Randomly, <a href=\"https://2.bp.blogspot.com/-epHyHyuvATc/UCeybwsrXbI/AAAAAAAAJ6E/Vx0pVi2v0Kg/s1600/DSC02874.JPG\" target=\"_blank\">Conan vs a Shoggoth</a> - ugh, so dumb-cool. <br /> <br /> From the farthest tunnel it arrives....the size of a pirate galleon... dripping and thundering, a luminiscent mass, alive in its most primitive.... changing form moment-to-moment, sickly eyes appearing and vanishing, like green-light postules... all the while screaming TEKELI-LI. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul_porpoise</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219803#post1219803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to shooting down the arguments, you made the extraordinary claim, you bring the alleged proof and I'll tell you if it's worth anything, but I'm not going to go through the entirely of Cornish culture and how it doesn't match Dorne</div> </div> </div> </div>Your objections are noted, friend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> And you are correct - you are not required to overview Cornish culture. You are not required to do anything at all.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> ...but please don't be surprised nor upset <b>then </b>if people can't differentiate Cornish people from anything else. <br /> <br /> If the experts on Cornwall huff-up at the non-Brits and exclaim &quot;well, you should know better!&quot; - and seem increasingly bothered by inquiries from non-Brits (who from the beginning, have admitted their ignorance - referring to online conversations in which the Cornish keep coming up) - then all I can do is shrug and move on to friendlier cultures. The planet is covered in peoples that are <i>eager</i> to make themselves known. Cornish-people aren't required to be one of them. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>My deepest apologies</b></span> for looking online and thinking Cornwall was relevant. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>I hope I didn't offend you</b> </span>by expressing curiosity and welcoming your insight on the region.<br /> <br /> ...and I hope this isn't taken as a lack-of-effort. English is neither my primary nor secondary tongue - and my posts would be error-laden if not for spellczech. So it's <b>not as if an effort isn't being made</b> when I go online trudging back-and-forth to see English people quibbling about English history (<i>that is incredibly foreign to me</i>). Dirty confession - stories with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shango\" target=\"_blank\">Chang\u00f3</a> were probably more relevant to my upbringing than Shakespeare. Not every English-speaker is an Anglophile.<br /> <br /> Wishing you a fantastic weekend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> P.S. More arbitrary online posts to confuse us foreigners - <a href=\"https://www.houseofnames.com/dorne-family-crest/English\" target=\"_blank\">Dorne is a Cornish Family Name</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T06:15:06-07:00","id":1219942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219931#post1219931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your objections are noted, friend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> And you are correct - you are not required to overview Cornish culture. You are not required to do anything at all.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> ...but please don't be surprised nor upset <b>then </b>if people can't differentiate Cornish people from anything else. <br /> <br /> If the experts on Cornwall huff-up at the non-Brits and exclaim &amp;quot;well, you should know better!&amp;quot; - and seem increasingly bothered by inquiries from non-Brits (who from the beginning, have admitted their ignorance - referring to online conversations in which the Cornish keep coming up) - then all I can do is shrug and move on to friendlier cultures. The planet is covered in peoples that are <i>eager</i> to make themselves known. Cornish-people aren't required to be one of them. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>My deepest apologies</b></span> for looking online and thinking Cornwall was relevant. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>I hope I didn't offend you</b> </span>by expressing curiosity and welcoming your insight on the region.<br /> <br /> ...and I hope this isn't taken as a lack-of-effort. English is neither my primary nor secondary tongue - and my posts would be error-laden if not for spellczech. So it's <b>not as if an effort isn't being made</b> when I go online trudging back-and-forth to see English people quibbling about English history (<i>that is incredibly foreign to me</i>). Dirty confession - stories with <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shango&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Chang\u00f3</a> were probably more relevant to my upbringing than Shakespeare. Not every English-speaker is an Anglophile.<br /> <br /> Wishing you a fantastic weekend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> P.S. More arbitrary online posts to confuse us foreigners - <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.houseofnames.com/dorne-family-crest/English&amp;quot;]Dorne</a> is a Cornish Family Name[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I say you should know better? <br /> <br /> I asked for any evidence to support the claim and said if you provide some then I'm happy to debate it and discuss it's veracity. <br /> <br /> And you doubled down on conflating Wales and Cornwall after I pointed out the error there, so if I'm unfriendly it because you made an innocent mistake (conflating Wales and Cornwall and trusting the internet) I pointed out it's incorrectness and then you kept doing it. <br /> <br /> And two links is hardly constantly coming up, I could post a quora question about whether Numenor is based off Australia as they are both islands with monarchs, that doesn't make it a common argument. <br /> <br /> We're a very friendly culture if you don't emmett-splain to us. <br /> <br /> Dorne isn't a name I've ever heard of or encountered, which doesn't mean much but nor does it show up in any lists of Cornish surnames and it doesn't follow the Tre, Pol or Pen pattern of a lot of Cornish names. Ah, it's Anglo-Norman so not Cornish at all, the family may never have even visited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5001-soul_porpoise","name":"soul_porpoise","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T08:46:50-07:00","id":1219978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219931#post1219931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but please don't be surprised nor upset <b>then </b>if people can't differentiate Cornish people from anything else.<br /> <br /> If the experts on Cornwall huff-up at the non-Brits and exclaim &quot;well, you should know better!&quot; - and seem increasingly bothered by inquiries from non-Brits (who from the beginning, have admitted their ignorance - referring to online conversations in which the Cornish keep coming up) - then all I can do is shrug and move on to friendlier cultures. The planet is covered in peoples that are <i>eager</i> to make themselves known. Cornish-people aren't required to be one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry but this doesn't resemble the exchange that's taken place in a way that just seems deeply disingenuous in context.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:30:02-07:00","id":1220015,"title":"","content":"I wanted to respond sooner - but work has been hectic today.<br /> <br /> Sorry if it sounds disingenuous - perhaps the fault is in the medium - gods know online-text lacks tone?<br /> <br /> But I was sincere in my earlier invitations. George R.R. Martin has painted Westeros as a continent-sized version of the Isles - so clueless as one is - one is inclined to believe online conversations where people point to-and-fro to different people living on those isles. Rather than chain-post links (to hear &quot;rejected, rejected, rejected&quot;) - it'd be dope to get a brief idea of what would be considered <i>essential</i> to look for? I've already agreed with Iozz-Sothoth's post (which I thought was super helpful).<br /> <br /> <b>Tangent: </b>Is there a better term for (people from the whole region)? Is &quot;British&quot; really the demonym for the entire United Kingdom? &quot;For us&quot;, we can variously use Latin &gt; Hispanic / Iberian &gt; Spanish &gt; Provincial identities (including Latin America). <b>But for the Isles</b>, I feel like conflating &quot;everyone&quot; with British is what makes part of this so confusing. <hr /><br /> I'm trying to figure out &quot;emmett-splain&quot; but <a href=\"https://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=Emmett\" target=\"_blank\">Urban Dictionary</a> doesn't seem right - and I see German, Irish, English and Hebrew listed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am doomed. <hr /><br /> By way of example, if I gave an overview of Iberia - I'd skip the 55 provinces - and reduce it to:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>North - </b>Latinized Celts in Forested Mountains - isolated.</span><ul><li>Basque (NE pagan druids), Galicians (NW semi-pagan barbarians), Asturians (christian paladins)</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>East - </b>Business-minded French/Italian/Spanish soldiers - road to Europe.</span><ul><li>Catalonia, Valencia, Aragon - where Celts, Romans, Visigoths, Moors &amp; Christians butchered each other. Red &amp; Gold are their colors.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>South </b>- Mediterranean mix. </span><ul><li>Andalusia. Islamic architecture but super-Catholic. Biggest grudge vs the Moors.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>West</b> - Independent, Sailors, 'manly men'.</span><ul><li>Portugal. If the East is defined by &quot;war comes to us&quot;, then the West is &quot;we seek out war&quot;.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Center</b> - generic Spanish &quot;peacocks&quot; who hate each other.</span><ul><li>Madrid. They like to think they brought civilization to everyone else - but are aware the other regions (not just Catalonia) are tempted to split off. Unity is less about &quot;common bonds&quot; and more about &quot;common ancestral foes&quot;.</li> </ul>Bam.<br /> <br /> Skip 2,000 years of history and 55 regions.<br /> <br /> Start with <b>Celts, Mediterraneans, Soldiers, Sailors, Centrists </b>- and I can contextualize a bunch of other random shit.<br /> <br /> <b>This</b> is what guess I'm vying for with the isles. I have a sense of &quot;Irish&quot; and &quot;Anglo&quot; - but Welsh, Scots, Cornish, etc are hard to put a finger on.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 05-18-2018, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:59:58-07:00","id":1220022,"title":"","content":"Two links to help with the current exchange-<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmet_(Cornish\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmet_(Cornish</a>)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burden_of_proof_(philosophy\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burden...of_(philosophy</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T12:26:38-07:00","id":1220059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1220022#post1220022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two links to help with the current exchange-<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmet_(Cornish\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmet_(Cornish</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1220022#post1220022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burden_of_proof_(philosophy\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burden...of_(philosophy</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, I think we're all on the same page?<br /> <br /> I never said &quot;it's (anyone's) obligation to prove this wrong&quot;. I already agreed - a while back - when the initial rebuttals came. I then wrote:<ul><li>I said: &quot;Maybe we'll get lucky and see more regional posts there.&quot;</li> <li>And when Iozz-Sothoth shared, I wrote: &quot;You rock.&quot;</li> <li>And to soul_purpoise: &quot;please feel free to share your insight! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;</li> </ul><b>Am I speaking the wrong kind of English?</b><br /> <br /> How does expressing that we'd be &quot;lucky&quot; to see more Cornish or Welsh info...<br /> How does expressing gratitude on a thought-out rebuttal listing ways the language/politics don't fit...<br /> How does expressing an interest in soul_purpoises insight on the region....<br /> <br /> ....equate to still trying to push the initial claims?<br /> <hr /><br /> This is where I get confused. Why does it consistently feel like English-speakers think conversations are a fight? I accepted the rebuttals as soon as they came in - then I tried to show interest in more info (since the Isles are the chief inspiration for the show). Patiently - and irritably - I thought it was clear I was interested in how locals differentiate themselves from each other (independent of their fantasy-spinoffs). I've never needed to ask someone (or rephrase myself) so many different ways to get a Peruvian or Trinidadian or Syrian to talk about themselves. lol<br /> <br /> I'll leave this as a &quot;final attempt&quot;. Regardless of reply, wishing you all a fabulous weekend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T13:34:50-07:00","id":1220079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Tangent: </b>Is there a better term for (people from the whole region)? Is &quot;British&quot; really the demonym for the entire United Kingdom? &quot;For us&quot;, we can variously use Latin &gt; Hispanic / Iberian &gt; Spanish &gt; Provincial identities (including Latin America). <b>But for the Isles</b>, I feel like conflating &quot;everyone&quot; with British is what makes part of this so confusing. </div> </div> </div>British covers everyone from Great Britain (as in, the specific large island where England, Wales and Scotland are). &quot;The UK&quot; is short for the &quot;United Kingdom of Great Britain <i>and</i> Northern Ireland&quot;, as Northern Ireland is on a separate piece of land.<br /> So people from the UK are mostly British, but some are Irish (or... Ulster Scots, Ulstermen, etc. Who live in Northern Ireland but are a seperate ethnic group to the Irish). And I guess there are other, much smaller islands around the UK, with their own ethnic groups who you could argue are British or not British (like the Manx), but their populations are small enough that you probably don't need to remember that.<br /> Basically, if you say British+Irish, that will cover everything you'll feasibly need, unless people are feeling awkward.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <br /> Perhaps we should move on, and go back to the original OP?<br /> <br /> So, the OP was about how Conan was very Exalted-esque.<br /> What other pulp fantasy would you recommend as Exalted inspiration?<br /> <br /> I'd suggest (though it's a little later) Elric of Melnibone. Exalted's sorcery is quite Elric-esque (as a reaction against DnD-esque magic), for example.<br /> <br /> For 2nd ed, I'd recommend maybe Hawkmoon (by the same author as Elric), but perhaps not for 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> Other pulp fantasy... I do like Lankhmar, but I'm not sure how well it fits Exalted. Somewhat, but I think Ffard and the Grey Mouser are more DnD characters than Exalted characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-18-2018, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T13:57:04-07:00","id":1220084,"title":"","content":"Wasn't trying to be combative or prolong anything, just thought maybe it was lost in translation, because your response wasn't exactly the most genteel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219931#post1219931\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219931#post1219931\"> The Conan books read like an Exalted game - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219931#post1219931\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1219931#post1219931 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I know, this isn't news. It's not like the Conan books haven't been referenced throughout the history of the line. Most relevantly there was the third edition statement that the sorcery rewrite was heavily influenced by them. \u200bBut I'd never exposed myself to Conan aside from the movies (when they came out, I'm not as young as all that). I recently found a complete e-book collection for $0.99, and I've read the first few novellas. I was shocked at how well everything, yes everything, in the books fit within scope and tone of Exalted. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm woefully under-read when it comes to pulp, so I'll just bow out of the original conversation; I was just trying to smooth over some confusion. /lurk","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T14:45:31-07:00","id":1220094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1220079#post1220079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps we should move on, and go back to the original OP?</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have been living in a cave - but a friend just linked me this:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mzubhJpbUK8\" target=\"_blank\">Conan Exiles - Cinematic Trailer</a>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So somewhat fittingly - Conan rescues the player-character (in the cinematic, a female) - but the video then asks what <b>your</b> story will be. Now I'm devouring videos while working on ads. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T15:52:00-07:00","id":1220121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1220059#post1220059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Except, I think we're all on the same page?<br /> <br /> I never said &amp;quot;it's (anyone's) obligation to prove this wrong&amp;quot;. I already agreed - a while back - when the initial rebuttals came. I then wrote:<ul><li>I said: &amp;quot;Maybe we'll get lucky and see more regional posts there.&amp;quot;</li> <li>And when Iozz-Sothoth shared, I wrote: &amp;quot;You rock.&amp;quot;</li> <li>And to soul_purpoise: &amp;quot;please feel free to share your insight! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&amp;quot;</li> </ul><b>Am I speaking the wrong kind of English?</b><br /> <br /> How does expressing that we'd be &amp;quot;lucky&amp;quot; to see more Cornish or Welsh info...<br /> How does expressing gratitude on a thought-out rebuttal listing ways the language/politics don't fit...<br /> How does expressing an interest in soul_purpoises insight on the region....<br /> <br /> ....equate to still trying to push the initial claims?<br /> <hr /><br /> This is where I get confused. Why does it consistently feel like English-speakers think conversations are a fight? I accepted the rebuttals as soon as they came in - then I tried to show interest in more info (since the Isles are the chief inspiration for the show). Patiently - and irritably - I thought it was clear I was interested in how locals differentiate themselves from each other (independent of their fantasy-spinoffs). I've never needed to ask someone (or rephrase myself) so many different ways to get a Peruvian or Trinidadian or Syrian to talk about themselves. lol<br /> <br /> I'll leave this as a &amp;quot;final attempt&amp;quot;. Regardless of reply, wishing you all a fabulous weekend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm prepared to write off as a hilarious miscommunication if you are. <br /> <br /> The quick summary of Cornwall (and to a large degree Devon next door) all comes back to tin and the sea. Tin mining in Cornwall and Devon was so essential to the state that tin miners were granted the right to form statuary parliaments who had the power to ratify or not any laws passed by the government upcountry and miners were immune to prosecution for the majority of crimes apart from by their own parliaments. Cornwall and Devon repeatedly revolted not at the behest of the local aristocracy but to resist attempts by London to back out of these deals. The dark side of this is Cornish miners once they had moved abroad were notorious scabs, since they had run their rights without the aid of others, they often saw no need to unionise. <br /> <br /> Those who weren't miners were fishermen, pirates, smugglers and wreckers. To this day, any ship that goes down in the west country will have locals descend from far and wide to grab what they can as salvage and ships still slip in at strange hours to dump cheap booze and drugs. <br /> <br /> These days the tin and fish are gone and most job prospects are part time holiday work or pissing off to another part of the UK with a better economy. <br /> <br /> But the most important part of Cornish identity is feuding with Devon and not trusting anyone from upcountry be they from London, Wales, Scotland, the moon or wherever. <br /> <br /> Does that help? <br /> <br /> <br /> You say you have a sense of Anglo? What is it? Not trying to start another disagreement, but the differences between the regions are still massive for such a small island. There's not many traits that I'll say are common to say Yorkshire and Essex for example. <br /> <br /> To make Oz happy, I'll add something relevant to the actual thread title. I often prefer to steal from Howard's Bran Mak Morn stories, less racism, more fighting an empire and Bran like any player makes truly questionable calls pretty constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5001-soul_porpoise","name":"soul_porpoise","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T17:02:55-07:00","id":1220133,"title":"","content":"Lord Dunsany was pretty awesome not <i>just</i> for <i>The Gods of Peg\u00e4na</i>, but also <i>The Fortress Unvanquishable, Save for Sacnoth</i>. <br /> <br /> Keep an eye out, when reading it, for Wong Bongerok. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T07:08:56-07:00","id":1220247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1220015#post1220015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if it sounds disingenuous - perhaps the fault is in the medium - gods know online-text lacks tone?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me it's the dancing around between topics, only two pages ago you were arguing against representation in fantasy novels because it might be unwelcome by some members of the group in question. It makes what transpired after that look less like an honest mistake and more an attempt to illustrate why talking about other cultures is a minefield. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T10:24:13-07:00","id":1220275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1220079#post1220079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other pulp fantasy... I do like Lankhmar, but I'm not sure how well it fits Exalted. Somewhat, but I think Ffard and the Grey Mouser are more DnD characters than Exalted characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>To launch into this tangent, yeah, sort of D&amp;D, sort of not in my book - on the one hand they set the mold for the picaresque adventuring of D&amp;D (fairly &quot;low&quot; characters who meet up in some tavern and taking some job), on the other, absolutely no adherence to character classes, they don't really fight monsters as part of a team so much as swashbuckle with other human individuals, and Leiber really cares more about jokes, comedy, irony, character, satire and fun than conquering dungeons and acquiring artifacts and gold (though maybe that's more D&amp;D than I think!).<br /> <br /> Exalted like characters actually feel fairly thin on the ground in most of what is described as S&amp;S - histories, epics, chanbara / jideigeki / wuxia and more thoughtful heroic fantasy anime pieces (Princess Mononoke, etc.) seem if anything a bit more fruitful. S&amp;S or pulp maybe more influential in terms of how the world feels.<br /> <br /> Terminology is a funny one here though, like, much of what Moorcock has done, strictly speaking he described as Epic Fantasy, simply with a different take than Tolkein and didn't construe it as S&amp;S simply from his world building being a bit more unusual and less self consciously evoking a mythic past and the morality a bit less clear cut; Hawkmoon, which I believe he called Epic Fantasy, is probably more useful for Exalted than Elric, which more arguably is S&amp;S. (Wizard, I'm guessing the magitech thing is why it's not so useful for 3e in your book?).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T14:12:38-07:00","id":1220331,"title":"","content":"Yeah, basically. Hawkmoon is a really good picture of a magitech-orientated fantasy world, but that works less well for 3rd ed than Wuxia and so on does (as you say).<br /> <br /> Elric specifically (ie Elric himself) is a good Solar character (he's a powerful sorcerer who makes pacts with spirits, has epic adventures, has the weapon that the Soulsteel Axe in Arms is based off, etc), but there aren't really any other Exalts in it, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> But anyway, I agree with you: S+S often has worlds similar to Exalted, but the characters are very low key.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T15:28:39-07:00","id":1220349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212634-the-conan-books-read-like-an-exalted-game?p=1220079#post1220079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like Lankhmar, but I'm not sure how well it fits Exalted. Somewhat, but I think Ffard and the Grey Mouser are more DnD characters than Exalted characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lankhmar is already kind of in Exalted, in the form of Nexus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T01:44:08-07:00","id":1220468,"title":"","content":"I meant the books generally, rather than the city.<br /> I think the setting generally works, but the characters aren't Exalted.<br /> <br /> (Honestly... I also don't feel Nexus fits Exalted very well, but there you go.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-20-2018, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}